{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system","id":1387071,"title":"Naval combat system","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-09T13:57:42-07:00","id":1387071,"title":"Naval combat system","content":"Hey has anybody used the naval combat system? To me it looks like the person with the biggest dice pool basically emerges unscratched while everyone else is at the bottom of the ocean. The solar sail charms seem to make this vastly worse. <br /> <br /> Is this inaccurate? I'm interested in play experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T14:06:30-07:00","id":1387074,"title":"","content":"DrLoveMonkey has.<br /> <br /> And I think that is indeed how he said he found it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T14:07:47-07:00","id":1387075,"title":"","content":"I've found that to be a very accurate description. Especially before the DB book where there was no, nada, any antagonist you could have that seemed to be able to anywhere near match a Solar except a Solar.<br /> <br /> The only way I can see a Solar not having an easy time of it is if they face off literally 6v1 or more due to the mounting outnumbered penalty. Even then the enemy captains would have to be very skilled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T14:28:59-07:00","id":1387081,"title":"","content":"You ever do a fight between a Solar Captain and a Lunar Kraken? I wonder how that would go.<br /> <br /> Tbh, it may just be the issue that always happened in early 3rd ed when there was basically Solars, mortals, and a few spirits, and nothing else.<br /> <br /> Even now you've the most powerful Exalts in Creation (the Solars), the weakest (Dragonblood), and a reasonably powerful kind for whom Sail is one of their weakest areas (Lunars).<br /> <br /> It's not like you can really do a naval battle between, say, a Solar captain and an Infernal, Abyssal or Sidereal captain (all Celestials who, unlike Lunars, actually have Sail charms).<br /> <br /> I wonder also if the Naval Combat system is much more fun for a Dragonblood game, where you can do fun things with Manouevres (with charms like making fog, ramming the **** out of other ships, shooting fire, etc) rather than just get a ton of successes and win.<br /> <br /> Same way 2nd ed combat was much more fun with Dragonblood than with Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T14:37:01-07:00","id":1387082,"title":"","content":"Yeah my read of db charms seemed like they were much more reasonable than solar charms, with actual interesting effects outside of &quot;insert motes, win battle&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T14:40:10-07:00","id":1387083,"title":"","content":"That is often the case between DBs and Solars, tbh.<br /> <br /> But at least with combat, it goes back and forth, there's lots of different things going on, lots of variables, probably plenty of cool stunts, so it doesn't just feel like &quot;make 2-3 opposed rolls, oh look you won&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T14:50:25-07:00","id":1387085,"title":"","content":"The lack of actual Lunar Sail pushed me to start writing up a small handful of Charms for that very purpose, intended to also be usable if you're being a Kraken and thus able to act as a naval combatant all on your own. I wonder if we'll eventually see nautical Lunar Charms crop up in Hundred-Faced Strangers, whether as backer Charms or just stuff that got squeezed out because wordcount.<br /> <br /> I agree that often, Solar Charms can feel a little heavy for the system and seem to sort of let you just... leap over chunks of it, whereas DB and even Lunar Charms feel like they actually interact with the system more. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T15:26:38-07:00","id":1387094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1387082#post1387082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah my read of db charms seemed like they were much more reasonable than solar charms, with actual interesting effects outside of &quot;insert motes, win battle&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair notice, I haven't actually played with the DB charms, and there's a lot of new powerful ones in Heirs. That being said, I do think that like a lot of DB stuff, it's a lot more in scale with a lot more of the world, and especially with the signature charms opens up a lot of cool things without being insta-wins.<br /> <br /> That being said, you're still going to struggle or have to make shit up to properly challenge a DB captain. They can easily take a three on one against enemy ships.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T16:00:18-07:00","id":1387110,"title":"","content":"I'll just note that with the rules such as they are, it also means artifact warship like the one in Arms really aren't worth much compared to being the guy with Salty Dog + Immortal Mariner against someone without. Some extra hull levels and extra damage on broadsides aren't going to save you if you can't get the momentum to fire them and wouldn't hit anything even if you did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T16:11:46-07:00","id":1387114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1387110#post1387110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll just note that with the rules such as they are, it also means artifact warship like the one in Arms really aren't worth much compared to being the guy with Salty Dog + Immortal Mariner against someone without. Some extra hull levels and extra damage on broadsides aren't going to save you if you can't get the momentum to fire them and wouldn't hit anything even if you did.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was something that I was concerned about as well. Artifact ships can of course get evocations, but unless they're at the level of &quot;this Evocation gives you Momentum&quot; or &quot;this Evocation defeats X maneuver&quot; they aren't ever going to be available against a solar captain","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T16:49:42-07:00","id":1387120,"title":"","content":"I think it's telling that when someone pitted two mortal captain's against each other in naval combat, it took 100+ turns to resolve. Granted that's sinking the enemy ship (something that doesn't always happen in games) but for something to take that long is painful. I learned this back when I made my spaceship rules hack. I thought I could redeem but no it's broken from the very core. Lunars have no charms that interact with naval combat in the same way as there's simply no way you can make charms on a subsystem that doesn't work.<br /> <br /> IIRC the ST guide might have new sailing rules. Which is good, as nearly anything is better than the rules we currently have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1387081#post1387081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder also if the Naval Combat system is much more fun for a Dragonblood game, where you can do fun things with Manouevres (with charms like making fog, ramming the **** out of other ships, shooting fire, etc) rather than just get a ton of successes and win.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trust me: It ain't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T17:22:59-07:00","id":1387129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1387120#post1387120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's telling that when someone pitted two mortal captain's against each other in naval combat, it took 100+ turns to resolve.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm I guess the system starts to break down at low dice-pools. Still I'm surprised it went that long given that momentum only goes up except when you're attacking and the captain who lands the first hit should start gaining momentum faster thanks to opponent hull-damage penalties.<br /> <br /> I guess a rule that everyone gains 1 point of automatic momentum every turn could help to make sure attacks can happen minimum every 5 rounds for everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T18:02:58-07:00","id":1387136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1387120#post1387120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's telling that when someone pitted two mortal captain's against each other in naval combat, it took 100+ turns to resolve. Granted that's sinking the enemy ship (something that doesn't always happen in games) but for something to take that long is painful. I learned this back when I made my spaceship rules hack. I thought I could redeem but no it's broken from the very core. Lunars have no charms that interact with naval combat in the same way as there's simply no way you can make charms on a subsystem that doesn't work.<br /> <br /> IIRC the ST guide might have new sailing rules. Which is good, as nearly anything is better than the rules we currently have.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Trust me: It ain't.</div> </div> </div> </div>100+ turns!? Holy crap I didn't expect it to be THAT bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":8804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","user":"armyofwhispers","date":". 05-09-2020, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T18:33:50-07:00","id":1387144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1387120#post1387120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's telling that when someone pitted two mortal captain's against each other in naval combat, it took 100+ turns to resolve. Granted that's sinking the enemy ship (something that doesn't always happen in games) but for something to take that long is painful. I learned this back when I made my spaceship rules hack. I thought I could redeem but no it's broken from the very core. Lunars have no charms that interact with naval combat in the same way as there's simply no way you can make charms on a subsystem that doesn't work.<br /> <br /> IIRC the ST guide might have new sailing rules. Which is good, as nearly anything is better than the rules we currently have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you know if they rule that you spend momentum on maneuvers even when you lose the die roll, or if they allowed stunts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T07:21:24-07:00","id":1387483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1387129#post1387129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm I guess the system starts to break down at low dice-pools. Still I'm surprised it went that long...</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the only reason the solar set (Or even the DB set against most non-solars) is that such sets only mask and cover up how awful the subsystem is. A solar can basically trivially belt out however many successes needed for maneuvers, and it doesn\u2019t help that high numbers on the roll is the de-facto end all of sail. If you have such charms, the opponent cannot do shit to you.<br /> <br /> You could say combat is the same, but not really. Sail adds such an amount of dice trivially to the point where it\u2019s easier to skip, as the enemy as the enemy will never have a chance to do anything.<br /> <br /> It literally repeats one of the very problems we had in 3e: combat taking so long because of opposed rolls. The reason why WoD or FATE works with opposed rolls is because at least you can get some measure of measurable success.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1387136#post1387136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 100+ turns!? Holy crap I didn't expect it to be THAT bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither did I. I thought it was bad, but wew.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1387144#post1387144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you know if they rule that you spend momentum on maneuvers even when you lose the die roll, or if they allowed stunts?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was straight RAW between two mortal captains with the exact same dicepools of 8 dice. It was ran with a machine, as I doubt two humans could realistically stunt 100+ turns. But even if you allowed stunts it wouldn\u2019t matter. Both sides could easily get a level 1 stunt to bring it up to 10 dice, but you\u2019d still have the same problems.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T02:31:46-07:00","id":1389600,"title":"","content":"I'm the ST of a circle with a Sail Supernal Eclipse. We just had a naval battle that may help shed light on the situation. First, though I want to address this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1387110#post1387110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll just note that with the rules such as they are, it also means artifact warship like the one in Arms really aren't worth much compared to being the guy with Salty Dog + Immortal Mariner against someone without. Some extra hull levels and extra damage on broadsides aren't going to save you if you can't get the momentum to fire them and wouldn't hit anything even if you did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Person with a Daiklave but no combat charms loses to person with combat charms but no daiklave seems like a pretty fair comparison. It makes sense that the one with charms and excelencies will pull out a win. In fact, I hope that paradigm is true for every subsystem.<br /> <br /> So my Eclipse has finished the Sail tree, has an artifact imbued ship (NOT an artifact ship). He was on one ship, the other 3 solars were each on their own ship. They were attacked by 4 Imperial Triremes in the open sea, no weather effects or hazards, no rocks or coral or whirlpools. A total white room scenario. He destroyed one with a Broadside followed by a ram, destroyed the second with a ram quite easily, and by that time the Non-Sail Solars had boarded one ship and broadsided the remaining one.<br /> <br /> Momentum is gained by Positioning, which is just Wits+Sail+Maneuver (a stat boats have), its an opposed roll. You gain momentum from the difference in your rolls. It takes only 5 momentum to broadside your opponent, which is absurdly low for a Sail focused character who has 11 dice before charms and excellencies come out to play. A broadside attack does a flat 1 or 2 damage depending on your weaponry, and ships only have 3, 4, or 5 hull points. Two Broadside attacks is almost a certain victory for a Sail user.<br /> <br /> Ramming costs 7 momentum and it deals 1 damage + 1 for every 3 successes you beat your opponents roll by. This is the best tactic for great sailors to beat lesser sailors because of the bonus damage potential. The Eclipse scored 22 successes on this roll, and dealt and extra 5 damage for 6 total hull points sundered. That will instantly destroy and non artifact ship.<br /> <br /> But if you don't want to deal with that, just use a basic Boarding action for 8 momentum. Now its just a regular fight. Sail over.<br /> <br /> Honestly, where can I find this &quot;100 turns battle&quot;? I find it hard to believe that rolling two equivalent dicepools against each other cannot get to a difference of 5 so one can broadside the other, then the loser has a dice penalty and its basically a finished battle. Hell, at 8 momentum it literally <b><i>is</i></b> a finished battle because the ships stop and the melee starts.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Jeez, forum, help a Solar out a bit.<br /> <br /> Im gonna run the Mortals battle. Wits 3 Sail 3 Specialty 1 Maneuver 2. Dice pool 9<br /> <br /> 1) A: 3 successes, B: 4. Net 1 to B.<br /> <b>B has 1 Momentum</b><br /> <br /> 2) A:1 , B3, net 2 to B<br /> <b>B has 3 Momentum</b><br /> <br /> 3) A: 4, B: 5, net 1 to B<br /> <b>B has 4 momentum</b><br /> <br /> 4) A:2 B: 1, Net 1 to A<br /> <b>B has 3 Momentum</b><br /> <br /> 5) A:1, B: 5, net 4 to B<br /> <b>B has 7 momentum. </b><br /> <br /> <i>B attempts to Broadside</i><br /> <br /> 6) A: 3, B: 4<br /> B Broadsides, does 2 damage.<br /> B has 2 momentum<br /> A is at -2 dice<br /> <br /> We can see that B got a lot luckier with the dice then A, but turn 5 roll really handed this to B. This all took me about 5 minutes to roll, type, roll, type, etc. this would have been easy to do one on one in 2 minutes tops, and even still, <i>Exalted is not a system designed for Mortal to Mortal fighting. </i>How well are two men with swords in heavy armor going to slug each other back and forth before someone builds up enough to successfully decisive? How boring is it to run a no-charm, no-mote rolloff?<br /> <br /> I get where people are coming from- if you can't sail then you aren't going to be good in a naval fight- but this is <b>Exalted</b>. Someone is going to have a Sail pool with excellencies of 15+ if you are sailing. Someone is gonna have weather sorcery. Someone is gonna jump 2 range bands onto the enemy ship. Someone is going to set a sail on fire with a flaming arrow. Someone is going to <i>swim</i> up to the enemy ship and rip the rudder out. You are Exalted, you do the incredible everyday. Complaining that a Mortal v Mortal white room is unfulfilling like complaining that a Ferrari doesn't make a good tow truck.<br /> <br /> EDIT 2:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system#post1387071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey has anybody used the naval combat system? To me it looks like the person with the biggest dice pool basically emerges unscratched while everyone else is at the bottom of the ocean. The solar sail charms seem to make this vastly worse.<br /> <br /> Is this inaccurate? I'm interested in play experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, going back to the first post: yes, this is basically true. A Sail focused character with a big dicepool and charms is going to devastate anyone else on the sea, and quickly. Just like how a Dawn with combat charms is going to roll a bunch of mercenaries, a Night with Larceny charms can rob anybody, and a Twilight with Medicine can Heal anything. Exalted are really good at what they do. That's the point of the game.<br /> <br /> Before anyone @'s me though, Sail is opposed by Sail, so yes, it absolutely is unfair to anyone without Sail, unlike Larceny-Awareness or Brawl-Melee-Archery-MA-Other, there isn't really any variety in Sail builds <i><b><u>for combat</u></b></i>.<br /> <br /> <b>HOWEVER</b>, you said one really interesting thing:<i> [The Sailor] emerges unscratched while <b>everyone else</b> is at the bottom of the ocean. </i><br /> <br /> Unlike Initiative, Momentum is <b><i>non-transferable</i></b>. Any you build up attacking the Sea Sprite is lost if you switch to attacking the Wave Dancer. And, for every ship that gangs up on you, you lose -2 dice beyond the first on your opposed sail rolls. So 2 ships on 1 is going to be really rough for the Sail Solar, and 3 on 1 is going to cause you to tap deep into your charms and motes to avoid that <b>-4 </b>penalty! It's much harsher than Onslaught penalties. A Dawn can easily roll 3 regular soldiers, an Eclipse is going to have to buck up to beat three ships.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 05-18-2020, 06:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T08:48:51-07:00","id":1389674,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8830_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8830\" data-vbnamecard=\"8830\">Sorcerous Overlord</a> I appreciate the feedback here! I have a few questions about your combat with your circle vs the Imperial triremes. <br /> <br /> Was there any exalted on the opposing side? <br /> <br /> Did the opposing ships do want damage to your solars whatsoever? <br /> <br /> Did they ever win a roll-off?<br /> <br /> How did you deal with mote regeneration? <br /> <br /> You say your eclipse has a full sail tree. Have they ever used the charms preventing or repairing hull damage in your campaign to date? <br /> <br /> To address some of your other points: I haven't run a scenario myself, but I will point out that your mortal on mortal combat scenario assumes first age weaponry on the ship firing the broadside to be able to pull off 2 hull damage in one go. Furthermore, if A had won the roll in stage 6, you'd have started over again. I can easily see a combat going to 10, 20 or even 30 friends given matched opponents. You didn't even finish the combat that you proposed. Even with the -2, that fight could face proceeded as many turns again as you presented there. If a system creates a situation where either one side is a clear victor or it becomes a slog, I don't think that's a great system, regardless. <br /> <br /> Finally, your last point where you imply that three ships would be a significant challenge to one eclipse solar. Have you ever run such a scenario? As you pointed out yourself, an eclipse solar can get obscene numbers of successes in a turn. A -4 penalty doesn't really amount to much if the opposing ships can never get a shot off. <br /> <br /> Consider this: a solar sailor with Excellency, salty dog method, and imortal mariners advantage. Dice pool of 8. Opponents, three ships with mortal captains at dice pools of 7 each. <br /> <br /> Edit: redoing this combat as I screwed up momentum gain","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":8804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","user":"armyofwhispers","date":". 05-18-2020, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T09:07:19-07:00","id":1389677,"title":"","content":"So here's something else to consider re: dawn vs sail against three opponents- the dawn is going to be at -2 onslaught a good chunk of the time. The ship is at a -4 penalty. <br /> <br /> Both can spend Excellency to negate that penalty pretty easily. <br /> <br /> The fundamental difference between the systems is that if the dawn's opponents get good rolls, they can reduce the dawn's initiative even if the dawn consistently rolls better than them. The sailor's opponents must roll better than the solar on multiple different turns to be able to do anything to him. Plus every single one of the solar's Opponents have double the number of health levels as the ships, and are thus more difficult to kill. <br /> <br /> The difference in charms is that the sail charms are vastly cheaper to gain the same dice tricks, and the sailor gets to activate them AFTER the roll if they want. (There is no melee equivalent to salty dog method that permanently gives you exploding 6's on every sail roll forever. As far as I know, no other ability has this dice trick for free, since it's ridiculously OP )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":8804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","user":"armyofwhispers","date":". 05-18-2020, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T09:41:11-07:00","id":1389681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1389600#post1389600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) A: 4, B: 5, net 1 to B<br /> <b>B has 4 momentum</b><br /> <br /> 4) A:2 B: 1, Net 1 to A<br /> <b>B has 3 Momentum</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure this should be A has 1 Momentum, B has 4 momentum, <br /> <br /> &quot;Positioning (Roll: Wits + Sail + Maneuverability; Cost: None)\u2014The ship attempts to maneuver itself into a more favorable position to harm its adversary, whether by ramming them, raking them with arrows, boarding them, or whatever other tactic the captain has in mind. For each success by which the player exceeds her opponent\u2019s Naval Maneuver roll, she gains one point of Momentum.&quot;<br /> <br /> Nothing about someone who loses the positioning roll losing momentum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T10:37:40-07:00","id":1389696,"title":"","content":"Ok, him redoing the combat for the solar with two essence 1 charms and 8 dice vs the three mortals with 7 dice each. Let's do everyone in triremes +2 maneuverability, four levels of hull -1/-2/-4/incap. Solar always targeting A, all three other targeting solar<br /> <br /> Round 1: <br /> S: 12; A: 2, B: 6, C: 5<br /> Solar momentum 10<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> Solar attempts a ram<br /> S:11; A: 3, B: 9, C: 4<br /> Solar deals 3 hull damage to A<br /> Solar momentum 3<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> S: 9; A: 2,B: 4,C: 5<br /> Solar momentum 10<br /> <br /> Round 4:<br /> Solar attempts Broadside<br /> S: 13; A: 0,B:6 ,C:2<br /> A is sunk.<br /> Solar momentum:5<br /> <br /> I could continue from here but there's really no point. <br /> <br /> There's no possibility of the other ships taking out the solar. Two charm investment and you'd need a 4-1 or 5-1 matchup to make it an even fight. I rolled out the solar a bunch of times with that dice pool and the lowest I got was a 6. Out of about 15 rolls, the solar never once rolled lower than the average roll off the mortals. <br /> <br /> Note the solar isn't mote neutral through this. He's spending 10m a turn and getting back 5. However an essence 1 solar can still keep that up for a full 9 turns of combat. After that he has either already killed all three ships or he can &quot;only&quot; get three motes of Excellency, double nines and reroll 6's and 1's until they stop coming up. So he's still rolling 9 dice with a bunch of dice tricks against mortals rolling 9 dice with no tricks. <br /> <br /> So mote neutral he's still stomping these mortals. Again, this is a two charm dip into sail at Essence 1. Your premise that an eclipse needs to 'bulk up' against multiple ships does not seem to hold water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T18:17:03-07:00","id":1389804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1389674#post1389674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8830_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8830\" data-vbnamecard=\"8830\">Sorcerous Overlord</a> I appreciate the feedback here! I have a few questions about your combat with your circle vs the Imperial triremes.<br /> <br /> ]Was there any exalted on the opposing side?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of, they were fae puppets controled by a raksha noble. They had a dicepool of 12 though. (5+5+2)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Did the opposing ships do want damage to your solars whatsoever? </div> </div> </div>Yes they wanted to destroy the sholars ship and humiliate them. EDIT: I think the &quot;want&quot; is a typo. The enemy did attack the non-Sail Solars and did damage, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Did they ever win a roll-off? </div> </div> </div>Yes. It was a 4 on 4 battle, and the other Solars didn't have sail charms and relied on the crew's sail pool of 8, although Invincible Admiral Method gave them a large bonus. they only succeeded by ganging up on one ship at a time, 3 on 1. They also used some of their non-Sail abilities creatively so i gave them bonuses for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How did you deal with mote regeneration? </div> </div> </div>Just like combat, 5m per turn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You say your eclipse has a full sail tree. Have they ever used the charms preventing or repairing hull damage in your campaign to date? </div> </div> </div>Yes, a few times. ocean hazards are pretty easy to throw at a group playing in the West. Jagged rocks, whirlpools, fogsharks, hurricanes, Storm Mothers, Sea Monsters, etc. This particular fight also started with Fae Magicks dropping the Solars about 100 feet though the air (like the classic Looney Tunes &quot;run off a cliff without realizing it&quot;), which forced the Eclipse to spend willpower and motes to avoid starting the battle with damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To address some of your other points: I haven't run a scenario myself, but I will point out that your mortal on mortal combat scenario assumes first age weaponry on the ship firing the broadside to be able to pull off 2 hull damage in one go. Furthermore, if A had won the roll in stage 6, you'd have started over again. I can easily see a combat going to 10, 20 or even 30 friends given matched opponents. You didn't even finish the combat that you proposed. Even with the -2, that fight could face proceeded as many turns again as you presented there. If a system creates a situation where either one side is a clear victor or it becomes a slog, I don't think that's a great system, regardless. </div> </div> </div>Yes, Yes, and Yes. a fight between two mortals with no special resources and small dicepools jockeying for position could go on for quite a long time. Its a good thing then that Exalted is not about two mortals with no resources and small dicepools, which I addressed in my earlier post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally, your last point where you imply that three ships would be a significant challenge to one eclipse solar. Have you ever run such a scenario? As you pointed out yourself, an eclipse solar can get obscene numbers of successes in a turn. A -4 penalty doesn't really amount to much if the opposing ships can never get a shot off.<br /> <br /> Consider this: a solar sailor with Excellency, salty dog method, and imortal mariners advantage. Dice pool of 8. Opponents, three ships with mortal captains at dice pools of 7 each. </div> </div> </div>EDIT: In this specific example, the Sail Exalt is spending motes faster than they regenerate, against mortals. It's not a <i>significant </i>challenge, but it is causing them to spend resources. <br /> <br /> I get the feeling that people want me to say that Sail has a flaw wherein having excellencies and charms makes you a lot better than mortals. Yes, yes it absolutely does have that flaw, just like Craft, Melee, Larceny, Stealth, Athletics, Ride, Archery, War, Bureaucracy, Presence, Performance, Occult, Survival, Investigation, Awareness and any other skill do. Just to look at Melee, for example, you can &quot;just&quot; buy Excellent Strike and Fire and Stones Strike and completely squash any mortal, all the time, very easily, and for very few motes. Or Athletics with ISE and Thunder's Might to beat anyone in a contest of strength. I'm not sure what the point of coming back around to &quot;Sail is broken because Exalts always win against mundane foes&quot; is, because that is the <b><i>literal theme of <u>Exalted</u></i></b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1389681#post1389681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure this should be A has 1 Momentum, B has 4 momentum,<br /> <br /> &quot;Positioning (Roll: Wits + Sail + Maneuverability; Cost: None)\u2014The ship attempts to maneuver itself into a more favorable position to harm its adversary, whether by ramming them, raking them with arrows, boarding them, or whatever other tactic the captain has in mind. For each success by which the player exceeds her opponent\u2019s Naval Maneuver roll, she gains one point of Momentum.&quot;<br /> <br /> Nothing about someone who loses the positioning roll losing momentum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, my mistake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 05-18-2020, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T09:05:18-07:00","id":1389985,"title":"","content":"I think part of the problem is that for a long time, and still arguably now, there hasn\u2019t been a single published magical foe for Sail Supernals to fight. It\u2019d be like if the antagonist chapter stopped after Battle Ready Soldier.<br /> <br /> Only if you have WFHW and make up some Dragonblooded captains and face them off against that Solar will they actually meet a challenge, and even then only if outnumbered three or four to one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T10:03:43-07:00","id":1389995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1389674#post1389674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To address some of your other points: I haven't run a scenario myself, but I will point out that your mortal on mortal combat scenario assumes first age weaponry on the ship firing the broadside to be able to pull off 2 hull damage in one go. Furthermore, if A had won the roll in stage 6, you'd have started over again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tried really hard to read the rules in such a way that you don't lose the cost of your maneuver from failing the roll but I can't. Making this change seems like it would make low-power foes a bit more threatening without causing other problems.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1389804#post1389804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just like combat, 5m per turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, I can't find anywhere in the books that it says this. If someone wants to make naval combat tougher and involving tougher decisions for the exalted, removing mote regeneration would certainly be a way to go. On the other hand it probably raises the power levels of the ridiculously mote-efficient charms Salty Dog Method and Immortal Mariner's Advantage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1389985#post1389985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think part of the problem is that for a long time, and still arguably now, there hasn\u2019t been a single published magical foe for Sail Supernals to fight. It\u2019d be like if the antagonist chapter stopped after Battle Ready Soldier.<br /> <br /> Only if you have WFHW and make up some Dragonblooded captains and face them off against that Solar will they actually meet a challenge, and even then only if outnumbered three or four to one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree although you can always say the magic phrase &quot;abyssal equivalents of solar charms&quot;. But there should be sailing Abyssals, sailing demons, and sailing Fair Folk statted up.<br /> <br /> Although maybe the system also has other flaws that would come out in a battle between powerful but close-to-evenly-matched foes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T12:06:08-07:00","id":1390013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1389995#post1389995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree although you can always say the magic phrase &amp;quot;abyssal equivalents of solar charms&amp;quot;. But there should be sailing Abyssals, sailing demons, and sailing Fair Folk statted up.<br /> <br /> Although maybe the system also has other flaws that would come out in a battle between powerful but close-to-evenly-matched foes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Particularly in the edition that partially billed taped as \u201cyou know all those cool gods, elementals, demons, terrestrial exalted, fairies, automata, ghosts and monsters that used to mean nothing next to celestial might? Well now the setting matters!\u201d<br /> <br /> But also Solars, for the low low cost of two motes, get double 9s, disappearing 6s and disappearing 1s on their sail rolls. For another three motes they can get up to 3 non-charm bonus dice, and for another 2m you get Essence dice and Essence non-charm successes. Then for another 2m all your opponent\u2019s 1s count as 10s for you.<br /> <br /> We aren\u2019t even out of the Essence 1 charms yet. What on Creation\u2019s tempestuous seas would EVER warrant all this? That\u2019s not even factoring in the maneuver charms that automatically defeat enemy maneuvers, or deal bonus damage to already high damage attacks and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T15:44:51-07:00","id":1390084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390013#post1390013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Particularly in the edition that partially billed taped as \u201cyou know all those cool gods, elementals, demons, terrestrial exalted, fairies, automata, ghosts and monsters that used to mean nothing next to celestial might? Well now the setting matters!\u201d<br /> <br /> But also Solars, for the low low cost of two motes, get double 9s, disappearing 6s and disappearing 1s on their sail rolls. For another three motes they can get up to 3 non-charm bonus dice, and for another 2m you get Essence dice and Essence non-charm successes. Then for another 2m all your opponent\u2019s 1s count as 10s for you.<br /> <br /> We aren\u2019t even out of the Essence 1 charms yet. What on Creation\u2019s tempestuous seas would EVER warrant all this? That\u2019s not even factoring in the maneuver charms that automatically defeat enemy maneuvers, or deal bonus damage to already high damage attacks and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Leviathans warrant this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T03:17:45-07:00","id":1390240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390084#post1390084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leviathans warrant this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also being outnumbered by ships with superior maneuvering. In other words, the standard operating procedure for pirates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T06:49:12-07:00","id":1390277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390084#post1390084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Leviathans warrant this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they?<br /> <br /> Exalted has ship sized Elementals, twenty foot sea serpents, thirty foot armored fish, thirty foot crocodiles, forty foot sharks (in previous editions at least, alongside 90 foot whales), and monstrous octopi of Legendary Size. None of them <i>remotely</i> warrant this.<br /> <br /> Leviathan, the Lunar elder, probably doesn't warrant this (eyeballing the Fangs at the Gate Charms).<br /> <br /> Could you have some mile long, super monster? Sure, probably. But you have to invent it whole cloth especially to challenge your Essence 1 Solar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390240#post1390240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also being outnumbered by ships with superior maneuvering. In other words, the standard operating procedure for pirates.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd have to be pretty badly outnumbered. Not sure what pirate cutters are less manuerverable than merchant vessels.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, the Sail subsystem does not look fun to me. &quot;Insert motes to win, please ignore half the Solar Charms (and all DB Charms).&quot; I've not used it and have no intention of using it.<br /> <br /> But... I kinda agree with Sorcerous Overlord (not about mote generation, you clearly get 5m/hour): Solars are <i>supposed</i> to win <i>by being better</i>. Lack of cool sea monsters and awesome supranatural captains of legend is a bigger problem than &quot;every roll is a Clash you can't lose&quot;. And &quot;Solars are more powerful than mortals&quot; really is a default assumption to the game -- not a problem with the Sail system.<br /> <br /> There is, I concede, an issue in that the Solar is only the Captain on the vessel -- the crew are going to be mortals and there's a question of how much difference one person can realistically make. Your Solar might perfectly divine the enemy ship's weak-point but he's not personally firing the canon or steering the ship. So from that point of view, Solar dominance over momentum is possibly a stretch. And the Charmset is all over the place.<br /> <br /> But the generally principle of Solars walking over all opposition is pretty Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-20-2020, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T09:16:14-07:00","id":1390304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390084#post1390084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leviathans warrant this.</div> </div> </div> </div>They absolutely do not. The one leviathan we have published so far is the Armored Kraken and it has 8 dice to its Naval Maneuvers pool, with no dice tricks, and no bonus due to a Maneuverability score. It has some really cool naval maneuvers too. Living Anchor, where the ship gets snatched up in its tentacles, and the captain has to broadside or ram to blow off enough off the suckers to get free.<br /> <br /> That's awesome, but it's simply never going to happen. The Kraken has to beat the Solar sailor enough times with the Maneuver rolls to gather up to 10 momentum to even attempt it. That might sound doable, but that's winning against a far superior dice pool supplemented by dice tricks, by at least 2 successes, five times in a combat.<br /> <br /> This isn't a case of &quot;Ah, one of the mortals thinks they can play with the big boys, eh? *snaps fingers with a spark of perfect Solar divinity* Let's show them how wrong they are, shall we?&quot; It's a 100 foot long behemoth made of almost nothing but layers of titanic muscle and thick armored plates. In a game with a Solar sailor, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vEf0o01ghck\" target=\"_blank\">this monster isn't even worth breaking out the dice for</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390240#post1390240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also being outnumbered by ships with superior maneuvering. In other words, the standard operating procedure for pirates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of, yeah. Adversaries of the Righteous gave us The Bloodthirsty, an example fleet of pirate reavers. Their pilots tend to have about 7 dice to their pools, with no magic obviously, so you need to outnumber the Solar 3 to 1 before you even get equal to their basic unmodified dicepool. If you're solo facing down like 6-7 ships at once though, then absolutely you want all those crazy automatically successful Solar maneuvers and bazillion dice trick charms and stuff.<br /> <br /> I have no idea if that's feasible to run though, and I mean that. I've never personally had the experience, it might be really fast and simple, and if it is that's one possible way, although I'd really like there to be more ways to have a 1v1 or even a 2v1 seem reasonable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T11:22:21-07:00","id":1390342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390304#post1390304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This isn't a case of &quot;Ah, one of the mortals thinks they can play with the big boys, eh? *snaps fingers with a spark of perfect Solar divinity* Let's show them how wrong they are, shall we?&quot; It's a 100 foot long behemoth made of almost nothing but layers of titanic muscle and thick armored plates. In a game with a Solar sailor, <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vEf0o01ghck&quot;]this</a> monster isn't even worth breaking out the dice for[/URL].</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth pointing out here that Orlando Bloom here is pretty much how I view Solars.<br /> <br /> He perfectly predicts the Kraken... but is up in the rigging when he does it, and the mortal soldiers don't respond fast enough.<br /> <br /> Then, as the Kraken effortlessly destroys the ship, he dances completely untouched through the carnage. Because he's awesome. <br /> <br /> And let's remember that he's an expert blacksmith and a master swordsman -- he's not even a sailor by trade. He's a Twilight who took Sail 3 and Salty Dog Method because his dad was a pirate. If he's played enough to raise his Sail to 5, is sailing on the legendary Flying Dutchman, with Eclipse Jack Sparrow, Pirate Queen Elizabeth Swan and an elite crew of the damned who have been plying the waves for a century with the blessings of sea goddess Calipso THEN sure, not worth busting out the dice for an Armored Kraken.<br /> <br /> But some random newb with three Essence 1 Charms on a normal ship crewed by mortal nobodies shouldn't be completely unstoppable. Unstoppable for one regular mortal? Sure. But not the worst beasts in the sea. <br /> <br /> And miss me with ganging up six or seven Kraken to deal with a single Essence 1 Solar. We'll play on land.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-22-2020, 06:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T16:00:30-07:00","id":1390400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390304#post1390304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They absolutely do not. The one leviathan we have published so far is the Armored Kraken and it has 8 dice to its Naval Maneuvers pool, with no dice tricks, and no bonus due to a Maneuverability score. It has some really cool naval maneuvers too. Living Anchor, where the ship gets snatched up in its tentacles, and the captain has to broadside or ram to blow off enough off the suckers to get free.<br /> <br /> That's awesome, but it's simply never going to happen. The Kraken has to beat the Solar sailor enough times with the Maneuver rolls to gather up to 10 momentum to even attempt it. That might sound doable, but that's winning against a far superior dice pool supplemented by dice tricks, by at least 2 successes, five times in a combat.<br /> <br /> This isn't a case of &quot;Ah, one of the mortals thinks they can play with the big boys, eh? *snaps fingers with a spark of perfect Solar divinity* Let's show them how wrong they are, shall we?&quot; It's a 100 foot long behemoth made of almost nothing but layers of titanic muscle and thick armored plates. In a game with a Solar sailor, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vEf0o01ghck\" target=\"_blank\">this monster isn't even worth breaking out the dice for</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wow!<br /> <br /> It seems like there is a combination of a few different problems, compounding on each other:<br /> <br /> (1) The Armored Kraken's dice pool is just not big enough for what it's representing. If we have a sea captain who is skilled, but not exceptional (+6) in a trireme (+2) then they will be the equal of the kraken in maneuvering. Regardless of the naval combat system (unless it doesn't depend primarily on the naval maneuver roll but rather some other stat) this is going to make the kraken not a sufficiently imposing foe.<br /> <br /> (2) The naval combat system, unlike the ordinary combat system, means that foes that are a little weaker get shut down. In the ordinary combat system, even a weaker enemy will have a good chance of hitting with a couple withering attacks, or even a decisive, and using their cool powers.<br /> <br /> (3) The Sail Charms are probably a little too efficient compared to Charms in other Abilities that have opposed rolls (unlike Craft and Lore, say).<br /> <br /> I've been thinking a bit about how to adjust the naval combat system to deal with (2).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390342#post1390342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Worth pointing out here that Orlando Bloom here is pretty much how I view Solars.<br /> <br /> He perfectly predicts the Kraken... but is up in the rigging when he does it, and the mortal soldiers don't respond fast enough.<br /> <br /> Then, as the Kraken effortlessly destroys the ship, he dances completely untouched through the carnage. Because he's awesome.<br /> <br /> And let's remember that he's an expert blacksmith and a master swordsman -- he's not even a sailor by trade. He's a Twilight who took Sail 3 and Salty Dog Method because his dad was a pirate. If he's played enough to raise his Sail to 5, is sailing on the legendary Flying Dutchman, with Eclipse Jack Sparrow, Pirate Queen Elizabeth Swan and an elite crew of the damned who have been plying the waves for a century with the blessings of sea goddess Calipso THEN sure, not worth busting out the dice for an Armored Kraken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you thought about how to design a sailing system in exalted that would make crew / other Circle members sufficiently important?<br /> <br /> I have some vague imagining of a system with different &quot;stations&quot; that have to be filled, like navigation and weapons and such, which can each be filled by a PC/Exalt, or, if none is available, an ordinary crew, that each have to make their own rolls. It sounds really hard to do right, but even a mediocre version might still be more fun than the current system, at least in the case when all the players are on the ship together","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25834,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","user":"habitableexoplanet","date":". 05-20-2020, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T21:31:56-07:00","id":1390470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1389804#post1389804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sort of, they were fae puppets controled by a raksha noble. They had a dicepool of 12 though. (5+5+2)</div> </div> </div> </div>So a fair dice pool on them, but no charms to provide dice tricks or excellency?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1389804#post1389804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes they wanted to destroy the sholars ship and humiliate them. EDIT: I think the &quot;want&quot; is a typo. The enemy did attack the non-Sail Solars and did damage, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, &quot;want&quot; was a typo. I meant to ask if the Raksha had done any damage to the solars ships. The perils of posting from a phone with crappy autocorrect.<br /> <br /> To confirm, the Raksha did not damage to the Eclipse solar with the Sail specialty?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1389804#post1389804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. It was a 4 on 4 battle, and the other Solars didn't have sail charms and relied on the crew's sail pool of 8, although Invincible Admiral Method gave them a large bonus. they only succeeded by ganging up on one ship at a time, 3 on 1. They also used some of their non-Sail abilities creatively so i gave them bonuses for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>So from the description of the fight, your Solar circle would have actually been invincible if the only one rolling dice was the Eclipse solar vs the other 4 ships. He'd have a -6 penalty, but obscene dice pools and dice tricks, and the ability to flat out win in certain contests such as Ship-Breaker Method or Superior Positioning Technique. The battle would have definitely gone longer from only one ship, but I'd be very surprised if the Raksha did any damage against the Eclipse, even 4v1.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1389804#post1389804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just like combat, 5m per turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I assume as well, but AFAICT it's not explicit in the sail rules.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1389804#post1389804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, a few times. ocean hazards are pretty easy to throw at a group playing in the West. Jagged rocks, whirlpools, fogsharks, hurricanes, Storm Mothers, Sea Monsters, etc. This particular fight also started with Fae Magicks dropping the Solars about 100 feet though the air (like the classic Looney Tunes &quot;run off a cliff without realizing it&quot;), which forced the Eclipse to spend willpower and motes to avoid starting the battle with damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was it your Eclipse Solar taking any damage, outside of the dropping 100 feet? Or was this another case where if they'd all been on the same ship, they'd actually take less damage?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1389804#post1389804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, Yes, and Yes. a fight between two mortals with no special resources and small dicepools jockeying for position could go on for quite a long time. Its a good thing then that Exalted is not about two mortals with no resources and small dicepools, which I addressed in my earlier post.</div> </div> </div> </div>While true, I don't think you get why some of us have identified this as a problem.<br /> <br /> This isn't <i>just</i> mortal vs mortal. With the sail system as is you can have two evenly matched opponents and it'll just be a slog whether those are mortals with 6 dice vs another mortal with the same or two solars with the same charms. There's no equivalent of being able to out-fox your opponent with clever strategy even if you're throwing the same dice around. If they beat you on a round they do what they want and you don't. Same is true vice versa. It's a total dice supremacy situation.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1389804#post1389804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: In this specific example, the Sail Exalt is spending motes faster than they regenerate, against mortals. It's not a <i>significant </i>challenge, but it is causing them to spend resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Motes come back at 5/hour. You overspend for the first few turns to kill the first ship, then drop down to minor spending and destroy the next two. It would be <i>really</i> easy for this two-charm investment solar to come out of this combat at full motes. He could literally just choose to sit there and make positioning rolls against the last opponent until his motes came back and then finish the last ship whenever he wants to. The enemy ship has no hope of escape, and no hope of ever doing damage to the solar.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is that this combat isn't worth the time it takes to run. The mortals cannot beat him no matter what. No other system in Exalted even comes <i>close</i> to this amount of supremacy from TWO CHARMS.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1389804#post1389804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the feeling that people want me to say that Sail has a flaw wherein having excellencies and charms makes you a lot better than mortals. Yes, yes it absolutely does have that flaw, just like Craft, Melee, Larceny, Stealth, Athletics, Ride, Archery, War, Bureaucracy, Presence, Performance, Occult, Survival, Investigation, Awareness and any other skill do. Just to look at Melee, for example, you can &quot;just&quot; buy Excellent Strike and Fire and Stones Strike and completely squash any mortal, all the time, very easily, and for very few motes. Or Athletics with ISE and Thunder's Might to beat anyone in a contest of strength. I'm not sure what the point of coming back around to &quot;Sail is broken because Exalts always win against mundane foes&quot; is, because that is the <b><i>literal theme of <u>Exalted</u></i></b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being better than someone is not the same as being completely, utterly unbeatable by <i>everyone</i>.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that &quot;Exalted always win against mundane foes&quot; is not the same as &quot;Exalts with two charms always win against mundane foes&quot; You keep saying the first one, but solar sail fits into the second one.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T21:37:55-07:00","id":1390473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390400#post1390400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wow!<br /> <br /> It seems like there is a combination of a few different problems, compounding on each other:<br /> <br /> (1) The Armored Kraken's dice pool is just not big enough for what it's representing. If we have a sea captain who is skilled, but not exceptional (+6) in a trireme (+2) then they will be the equal of the kraken in maneuvering. Regardless of the naval combat system (unless it doesn't depend primarily on the naval maneuver roll but rather some other stat) this is going to make the kraken not a sufficiently imposing foe.<br /> <br /> (2) The naval combat system, unlike the ordinary combat system, means that foes that are a little weaker get shut down. In the ordinary combat system, even a weaker enemy will have a good chance of hitting with a couple withering attacks, or even a decisive, and using their cool powers.<br /> <br /> (3) The Sail Charms are probably a little too efficient compared to Charms in other Abilities that have opposed rolls (unlike Craft and Lore, say).</div> </div> </div> </div>These pretty much sum it up for me, though I think you`re under playing 3 here. Sail has no Essence 4 or 5 charms. It maxes out at Essence 3, and it gets scary powerful with minimum investment.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390400#post1390400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been thinking a bit about how to adjust the naval combat system to deal with (2).<br /> <br /> Have you thought about how to design a sailing system in exalted that would make crew / other Circle members sufficiently important?<br /> <br /> I have some vague imagining of a system with different &quot;stations&quot; that have to be filled, like navigation and weapons and such, which can each be filled by a PC/Exalt, or, if none is available, an ordinary crew, that each have to make their own rolls. It sounds really hard to do right, but even a mediocre version might still be more fun than the current system, at least in the case when all the players are on the ship together</div> </div> </div> </div>I`ve been working on an alternate sail system, and the ability for the non-sail champions on the crew to do something in a combat is high up on my priority list.<br /> <br /> Also should allow for things like trading broadsides (which is in like every naval movie ever), or for any ship outside the sail supernal to actually be able to have a turn at all. I`ll see about trying to post what I`ve got in the next few days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T21:52:29-07:00","id":1390478,"title":"","content":"The most successful ship based RPGs I've ever seen have been Star Trek Adventures and Rogue Trader, and they both operate almost exactly the same way, with different ship positions that all get to go once per turn if they're crewed, and all give either some benefit like allowing for communication, or buffing someone else's action like by using sensors to increase the accuracy of the weapons fire.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how well that will translate to Exalted, partially because there might be less fun obvious things to do without the sci-fi angle, and also because unlike those games Exalted might not have the right attribute/ability spread to fill multiple roles with characters with a variety of skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T21:57:53-07:00","id":1390480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390470#post1390470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He could literally just choose to sit there and make positioning rolls against the last opponent until his motes came back and then finish the last ship whenever he wants to. The enemy ship has no hope of escape, and no hope of ever doing damage to the solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth you could also do this in regular combat. How I treat it is if players are specifically just dicking around waiting for motes to regen and underspending when they could easily just win I end the combat and say &quot;Yeah, they flee, if you want to cut them down as they flee you may.&quot;<br /> <br /> I often even preempt that before the round even ends, if they explode and kill everyone but the last two guys, then on that very tick the round ends with their death/surrender.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T06:10:15-07:00","id":1390539,"title":"","content":"In terms of non-Sail things to do in different positions... the naval technology of the setting plus magic actually has a lot of options here because you can't just input commands into a computer and have the ship do stuff.<br /> <br /> Since Savage Seas is considered a lore appropriate book for 3e, we have a list of positions already (going to skip the under positions since I doubt you'd have enough PCs and important PCs to need all of those secondary positions having places to give bonuses):<br /> <br /> Admiral: The leader of multiple ships. War could be used for Command Actions and Strategic Warfare per the existing rules for those; maybe modified slightly.<br /> Captain: In many cases they're not actually sailing the ship, but organizing the crew, making their function more Presence or War oriented depending on the situation.<br /> Kubernetes: The actual pilot of the boat, this is where your best Sail person goes.<br /> Proreus: This is probably the most flexible of the command level part of the crew and oversees whatever the captain and kubernetes don't. Awareness (if the kubernetes is the conn, the proreus is sensors), Investigation (is the captain's main enforcer), Presence, or War (is responsible for crew discipline) depending on the skills of the rest would be important.<br /> Keleteus (only if the boat has oars): Performance and/or Presence to keep the rowers operating together; vital for getting the most speed you can out of your boat.<br /> Arms Master: Another War position that's done by the Proreus in smaller crews anyway, should also be the best fighter as the direct unit leader of armed forces in combat.<br /> Purser: Bureaucracy and Socialize primary as the one responsible for ship supplies. Navies sail on their stomachs too. Lore and Occult if the ship can't afford a specialist to negotiate with spirits.<br /> Carpenter, Weapon Smith, and Sailmaker: Crafts obviously.<br /> Surgeon: Medicine obviously.<br /> Master of the Tops and Master of the Bow (only if the boat has rigging; Master of the Bow would still exist on a rowed vessel but wouldn't be actively important in tense situations): Athletics as the crew that handle the rigging in a sailing vessel means a lot of agility and strength to ensure the sails are positioned properly, though both positions should also have good Awareness as they are relied on as spotters (esp. on large ships) due to their vantage points.<br /> <br /> And while not given any official title in that book:<br /> <br /> Ritualist: Occult and Lore. Ships in Exalted have lots of strange things to worry about that real world ones don't. Someone needs to know the way to appease the various spirits and gods the ship might encounter. Having an actual Sorcerer is even a bigger boost of course.<br /> <br /> So there's room for a lot of other Abilities to come to bear in ship operations. Though they overlap a lot in practical function, I think it's more than enough to fill out something like STA's base concept. Ignoring admirals:<br /> <br /> The CO stuff goes to the captain and proreus.<br /> The Helm and Navigation stuff goes to the kubernetes, keleteus, and masters of the tops and bow.<br /> Sensors go to the proreus and masters of the tops and bow.<br /> Security and Tactical go to the proreus and arms master.<br /> Comms goes to the purser and ritualist.<br /> Internal Systems go to the purser, craftsmen, and surgeon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T08:09:24-07:00","id":1390553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390480#post1390480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For what it's worth you could also do this in regular combat. How I treat it is if players are specifically just dicking around waiting for motes to regen and underspending when they could easily just win I end the combat and say &quot;Yeah, they flee, if you want to cut them down as they flee you may.&quot;<br /> <br /> I often even preempt that before the round even ends, if they explode and kill everyone but the last two guys, then on that very tick the round ends with their death/surrender.</div> </div> </div> </div>Edit: Sorry, i misread your post initially. <br /> <br /> I'd agree that as a ST it would make sense to just end combat and whatever result the solar wants to happen, just happens. They're in complete control of the situation. If they want the enemy sunk, it sinks. I don't think there's actually much point in toying with a ship for mote regen anyway since in Naval time scales, you're likely to get back a good chunk of your mote pool before the next encounter, if not all of it. Most of the time it takes hours to get anywhere with a sail. <br /> <br /> But to take that further, I don't think I'd even bother running the combat past the death of the first ship. When the enemy is down to two ships, I don't think it's likely for them to do even a single point of damage to the solar before being utterly destroyed. I don't think it was likely with 3 ships to do any damage to the solar, but at least there it's possible/forcing him to spend some motes to keep ahead.<br /> <br /> If this was 3 mortal ships vs a sail supernal with heavy investment in sail? I wouldn't bother with the combat at all. The solar just wins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":8804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","user":"armyofwhispers","date":". 05-21-2020, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T08:28:39-07:00","id":1390556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390539#post1390539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of non-Sail things to do in different positions... the naval technology of the setting plus magic actually has a lot of options here because you can't just input commands into a computer and have the ship do stuff.<br /> <br /> Since Savage Seas is considered a lore appropriate book for 3e, we have a list of positions already (going to skip the under positions since I doubt you'd have enough PCs and important PCs to need all of those secondary positions having places to give bonuses):<br /> <br /> Admiral: The leader of multiple ships. War could be used for Command Actions and Strategic Warfare per the existing rules for those; maybe modified slightly.<br /> Captain: In many cases they're not actually sailing the ship, but organizing the crew, making their function more Presence or War oriented depending on the situation.<br /> Kubernetes: The actual pilot of the boat, this is where your best Sail person goes.<br /> Proreus: This is probably the most flexible of the command level part of the crew and oversees whatever the captain and kubernetes don't. Awareness (if the kubernetes is the conn, the proreus is sensors), Investigation (is the captain's main enforcer), Presence, or War (is responsible for crew discipline) depending on the skills of the rest would be important.<br /> Keleteus (only if the boat has oars): Performance and/or Presence to keep the rowers operating together; vital for getting the most speed you can out of your boat.<br /> Arms Master: Another War position that's done by the Proreus in smaller crews anyway, should also be the best fighter as the direct unit leader of armed forces in combat.<br /> Purser: Bureaucracy and Socialize primary as the one responsible for ship supplies. Navies sail on their stomachs too. Lore and Occult if the ship can't afford a specialist to negotiate with spirits.<br /> Carpenter, Weapon Smith, and Sailmaker: Crafts obviously.<br /> Surgeon: Medicine obviously.<br /> Master of the Tops and Master of the Bow (only if the boat has rigging; Master of the Bow would still exist on a rowed vessel but wouldn't be actively important in tense situations): Athletics as the crew that handle the rigging in a sailing vessel means a lot of agility and strength to ensure the sails are positioned properly, though both positions should also have good Awareness as they are relied on as spotters (esp. on large ships) due to their vantage points.<br /> <br /> And while not given any official title in that book:<br /> <br /> Ritualist: Occult and Lore. Ships in Exalted have lots of strange things to worry about that real world ones don't. Someone needs to know the way to appease the various spirits and gods the ship might encounter. Having an actual Sorcerer is even a bigger boost of course.<br /> <br /> So there's room for a lot of other Abilities to come to bear in ship operations. Though they overlap a lot in practical function, I think it's more than enough to fill out something like STA's base concept. Ignoring admirals:<br /> <br /> The CO stuff goes to the captain and proreus.<br /> The Helm and Navigation stuff goes to the kubernetes, keleteus, and masters of the tops and bow.<br /> Sensors go to the proreus and masters of the tops and bow.<br /> Security and Tactical go to the proreus and arms master.<br /> Comms goes to the purser and ritualist.<br /> Internal Systems go to the purser, craftsmen, and surgeon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also have plans for things like an archery supernal to be able to essentially make their own broadside if the ships get close enough, or other ridiculous Exalt-level tasks that could be carried out depending on the circumstances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T09:20:12-07:00","id":1390560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390553#post1390553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If this was 3 mortal ships vs a sail supernal with heavy investment in sail? I wouldn't bother with the combat at all. The solar just wins.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you might need to go with like, 5-6 rather than 3. The upshot is that the outnumbered penalty doesn't count the caliber of ship you're facing, so two corsairs and four fast attack ships still count as a -10 penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T14:08:46-07:00","id":1390621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390556#post1390556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also have plans for things like an archery supernal to be able to essentially make their own broadside if the ships get close enough, or other ridiculous Exalt-level tasks that could be carried out depending on the circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing I would be careful with, is that boats big enough for serious naval combat need to function as well-oiled human-powered machines. However well the intention, an Exalt archer taking pot shots at enemies ships/crew could mess up their whole ship's operations.<br /> <br /> A Solar archer not working in coordination with the arms master (assuming they aren't the arms master and then need to be in coordination with the proreus and/or captain) can easily screw things up by &quot;helping.&quot; Lets say that Solar acting on their own decides to Charm up and obliterate the enemy ships main mast. That's pretty sweet, the enemy boat is either dead in the water or at least limping now, so boarding them will be simple. But this sets off a chain reaction if the rest of the crew didn't know it was going to happen. Boats don't stop and turn on a dime. One of the watchers needs to spot this, and relay it to the kubernetes. The kubernetes needs to toss out a bunch of orders on the fly. The proreus needs to make sure all those orders get to the right people. Those orders need to be executed perfectly in sync with each other. If a single step gets screwed up, the boarding action keeps derailed as the ship is nowhere near the crippled enemy boat instead of pulling up next to it. All because one super-archer decided to act on their own volition.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure this is why DrLoveMonkey was pointing towards something like STA's starship battle rules. You put that archer in as the arms master of the ship. They're normally busy running all of the ship's ranged fighters, with whatever bonuses that could provide. One of the CO positions could use their bonus to give the archer a bonus action, which they could use to do a big personal effect with; putting the coordination into the system and avoiding the chain reaction of events above.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T14:24:21-07:00","id":1390626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390473#post1390473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These pretty much sum it up for me, though I think you`re under playing 3 here. Sail has no Essence 4 or 5 charms. It maxes out at Essence 3, and it gets scary powerful with minimum investment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I'm inclined to agree - I just wanted to make some softer claims that would be harder to argue against, rather than say something more bold.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I`ve been working on an alternate sail system, and the ability for the non-sail champions on the crew to do something in a combat is high up on my priority list.<br /> <br /> Also should allow for things like trading broadsides (which is in like every naval movie ever), or for any ship outside the sail supernal to actually be able to have a turn at all. I`ll see about trying to post what I`ve got in the next few days. </div> </div> </div>I'm excited to see how your system turns out! I have a brief comment:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390539#post1390539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Captain: In many cases they're not actually sailing the ship, but organizing the crew, making their function more Presence or War oriented depending on the situation.<br /> Kubernetes: The actual pilot of the boat, this is where your best Sail person goes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that - because Exalted is a game not mainly built around sailing - the best Sail person will want to take the lead in a naval encounter (as compensation for their character's Sail pool not being relevant in other situations). Thus I think it might make sense to set up a system where the highest Sail person uses their naval expertise to decide what to do, and then informs the other officers, including a social role who distributes it to the wider crew. This might not even make a big mechanical difference if in practice the PCs decide on a strategy together and then implement it separately, but I think it's worth thinking about.<br /> <br /> On the other hand in a naval Exalted campaign maybe that's not so much of a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T14:59:23-07:00","id":1390632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390621#post1390621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing I would be careful with, is that boats big enough for serious naval combat need to function as well-oiled human-powered machines. However well the intention, an Exalt archer taking pot shots at enemies ships/crew could mess up their whole ship's operations.<br /> <br /> A Solar archer not working in coordination with the arms master (assuming they aren't the arms master and then need to be in coordination with the proreus and/or captain) can easily screw things up by &quot;helping.&quot; Lets say that Solar acting on their own decides to Charm up and obliterate the enemy ships main mast. That's pretty sweet, the enemy boat is either dead in the water or at least limping now, so boarding them will be simple. But this sets off a chain reaction if the rest of the crew didn't know it was going to happen. Boats don't stop and turn on a dime. One of the watchers needs to spot this, and relay it to the kubernetes. The kubernetes needs to toss out a bunch of orders on the fly. The proreus needs to make sure all those orders get to the right people. Those orders need to be executed perfectly in sync with each other. If a single step gets screwed up, the boarding action keeps derailed as the ship is nowhere near the crippled enemy boat instead of pulling up next to it. All because one super-archer decided to act on their own volition.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure this is why DrLoveMonkey was pointing towards something like STA's starship battle rules. You put that archer in as the arms master of the ship. They're normally busy running all of the ship's ranged fighters, with whatever bonuses that could provide. One of the CO positions could use their bonus to give the archer a bonus action, which they could use to do a big personal effect with; putting the coordination into the system and avoiding the chain reaction of events above.</div> </div> </div> </div>You raise some good points. <br /> <br /> While I would agree that this type of action <i>should</i> be coordinated with the leadership of the ship, I think there's gotta be some room for independent action simply because this is Exalted. Dawns gotta Dawn, Nights gotta Night, etc. <br /> <br /> I wasn't initially going to go with a 'stations' approach but I'm strongly considering it. Might have to allow for some amount of lateral action for that though. Play gets pretty boring if you can only do one thing, and you just do that repeatedly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T15:58:57-07:00","id":1390644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390626#post1390626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that - because Exalted is a game not mainly built around sailing - the best Sail person will want to take the lead in a naval encounter (as compensation for their character's Sail pool not being relevant in other situations).</div> </div> </div> </div>Narratively that's already how Savage Seas says a ship operates. The kubernetes is subordinate to the captain if they're not the same person, but once a battle breaks out, the kubernetes is effectively in command with the captain supporting them. The captain is still &quot;in charge&quot; in the sense of setting the goals for the ship, but the kubernetes has the responsibility and authority necessary to accomplish that goal; and the captain is supposed to stand aside and let them do it. Mechanically in 3e, it's just swapping the word &quot;captain&quot; in the naval combat rules to &quot;kubernetes,&quot; as the person that's actually doing the Sail rolls for the ship.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390632#post1390632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't initially going to go with a 'stations' approach but I'm strongly considering it. Might have to allow for some amount of lateral action for that though. Play gets pretty boring if you can only do one thing, and you just do that repeatedly.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC STA stations have 5 or 6 generic actions, and 4 to 6 station specific actions?<br /> <br /> Enough that each station has something to be doing that's not repetitive as long as the combat itself is interesting enough they all have things to be doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T23:59:24-07:00","id":1390719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390400#post1390400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wow!<br /> <br /> It seems like there is a combination of a few different problems, compounding on each other:<br /> <br /> (1) The Armored Kraken's dice pool is just not big enough for what it's representing. If we have a sea captain who is skilled, but not exceptional (+6) in a trireme (+2) then they will be the equal of the kraken in maneuvering. Regardless of the naval combat system (unless it doesn't depend primarily on the naval maneuver roll but rather some other stat) this is going to make the kraken not a sufficiently imposing foe.<br /> <br /> (2) The naval combat system, unlike the ordinary combat system, means that foes that are a little weaker get shut down. In the ordinary combat system, even a weaker enemy will have a good chance of hitting with a couple withering attacks, or even a decisive, and using their cool powers.<br /> <br /> (3) The Sail Charms are probably a little too efficient compared to Charms in other Abilities that have opposed rolls (unlike Craft and Lore, say).<br /> <br /> I've been thinking a bit about how to adjust the naval combat system to deal with (2).</div> </div> </div> </div>For once, I agree a published NPC is WAAAAY underpowered.<br /> <br /> (By and large NPC power blocks are just fine, but people horribly min-max their PCs. But this is just terri-bad.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390400#post1390400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you thought about how to design a sailing system in exalted that would make crew / other Circle members sufficiently important?<br /> <br /> I have some vague imagining of a system with different &quot;stations&quot; that have to be filled, like navigation and weapons and such, which can each be filled by a PC/Exalt, or, if none is available, an ordinary crew, that each have to make their own rolls. It sounds really hard to do right, but even a mediocre version might still be more fun than the current system, at least in the case when all the players are on the ship together</div> </div> </div> </div>Rogue Trader handles this passably well. As does Age of Rebellion. But those are for space ships in games about space ships.<br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> Ah another page. Yeah STA is also good -- better than AoR but I prefer RT -- it's probably over complicated for Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-22-2020, 03:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T02:46:01-07:00","id":1390738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390470#post1390470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a fair dice pool on them, but no charms to provide dice tricks or excellency?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's right. Our session this week was online due to Covid, and since we were about to take on the campaign-ending Leviathan (NOT Leviathan from Lunars, whose name is terribly inconvenient), I threw a side story at them. A Fae Noble wants them to fail. This battle was actually designed to be easy to beat- but drain the Eclipse of motes and willpower so he'd be weaker for the &quot;real&quot; challenge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, &quot;want&quot; was a typo. I meant to ask if the Raksha had done any damage to the solars ships. The perils of posting from a phone with crappy autocorrect.<br /> To confirm, the Raksha did not damage to the Eclipse solar with the Sail specialty? </div> </div> </div>That's right. They did not beat the Sail supernal. They didn't stand a chance (go ahead and quote me, forumites), becuase they are not Exalted themselves. They only damaged the ships commanded by the other Solars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So from the description of the fight, your Solar circle would have actually been invincible if the only one rolling dice was the Eclipse solar vs the other 4 ships. He'd have a -6 penalty, but obscene dice pools and dice tricks, and the ability to flat out win in certain contests such as Ship-Breaker Method or Superior Positioning Technique. The battle would have definitely gone longer from only one ship, but I'd be very surprised if the Raksha did any damage against the Eclipse, even 4v1. </div> </div> </div>Yes, which was intentional. The goal for this specific battle- mortals against a Supernal Exalted- was just to drain him of motes and willpower. this was the literal first thing they did in a 5 hour session. After that, the Fae Noble subjected them to individually tailored tests meant to give them Limit and force them to spend Willpower. The design goal of the session was to make them drained, off balance, and tired.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Was it your Eclipse Solar taking any damage, outside of the dropping 100 feet? Or was this another case where if they'd all been on the same ship, they'd actually take less damage </div> </div> </div>No, he didnt take any damage. A Supernal going 1 on 2 against talented mortals isn't anything but a speed bump. Mechanics aside, it was really fun though and the player had a great time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While true, I don't think you get why some of us have identified this as a problem.<br /> <br /> This isn't <i>just</i> mortal vs mortal. With the sail system as is you can have two evenly matched opponents and it'll just be a slog whether those are mortals with 6 dice vs another mortal with the same or two solars with the same charms. There's no equivalent of being able to out-fox your opponent with clever strategy even if you're throwing the same dice around. If they beat you on a round they do what they want and you don't. Same is true vice versa. It's a total dice supremacy situation. </div> </div> </div>I mean, on one hand I get it. You always want a dynamic system that rewards ingenuity and player agency. OTOH... look man I don't know how many times I can say that's just how Exalted works. if 2 people are gonna keep competing at each other without the system rewarded mechanics of Charms and Excellencies then the one with the bigger dicepool is just going to win. If one side stunts, the other stunts. it's a pure numbers game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not really. Motes come back at 5/hour. You overspend for the first few turns to kill the first ship, then drop down to minor spending and destroy the next two. It would be <i>really</i> easy for this two-charm investment solar to come out of this combat at full motes. He could literally just choose to sit there and make positioning rolls against the last opponent until his motes came back and then finish the last ship whenever he wants to. The enemy ship has no hope of escape, and no hope of ever doing damage to the solar. </div> </div> </div>So first I understand why you and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> argue for 5m/hour, but I feel that the Sailor making opposed sail rolls and maneuvers counts as a turn in combat. At my table that's the ruling. For your next point- Yes! it would be really easy for a Solar to spend only minimal motes and slowly chip away at his foes. You are right. Which is why, as a Storyteller, I don't let my players have it easy. There's literally hundreds of game design examples on how to challenge players to keep them from being careful and over-cautious. It didn't come up in my battle because my Sail supernal Eclipse goes hard and fast at everything, so he didn't need to be prodded with the stick. But if he sat back and tried to auto-win I would have made the battle harder with weather effects. <i>You might not think that's balanced</i>, and that's fine. STing is an inherently reactive process.<br /> <br /> If I had a Dawn with 15 combat charms, I'd start throwing harder enemies at the party. If I had a Night with Stealth and Larceny charms, they'd eventually run into a DB Sherlock. That doesn't make Sail balanced, I'm not saying it does, but you need to remember that Exalted is not a videogame that can be cheesed by tricking the AI.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What I'm saying is that this combat isn't worth the time it takes to run. </div> </div> </div>By all means, call my Sail Supernal Eclipse player and tell him that playing the invincible sailor and showing off is WrongBadFun. Tell my Twilight that exorcisms below 2nd circle demons are meaningless dice rolls. Not everything has to be a perfectly balanced challenge with meaningful stakes, letting your Exalts roflstomp something with their Supernal can be great fun <i>for the player</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The mortals cannot beat him no matter what. No other system in Exalted even comes <i>close</i> to this amount of supremacy from TWO CHARMS. <b>Being better than someone is not the same as being completely, utterly unbeatable by <i>everyone</i></b>. Not to mention that &quot;Exalted always win against mundane foes&quot; is not the same as &quot;<b>Exalts with </b><b><b>two </b>charms always win </b>against mundane foes&quot; You keep saying the first one, but solar sail fits into the second one. </div> </div> </div>Challenge Accepted<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Page 316- Flawless Pickpocketing Technique</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">With hands quicker than the eye, the Exalt relieves a<br /> hapless soul of his material burden. This Charm enhances<br /> a normal pickpocketing attempt (see p. 224). <b>Unless<br /> contested by magic, this attempt cannot fail; </b><br /> ...<br /> Characters using ordinary senses cannot detect this theft<br /> with Awareness. Characters with inhuman sensory acuity,<br /> such as a spider feeling vibrations in its web, or those using<br /> magic, like a Celestial Lion\u2019s Intemperate Gaze, suffer a<br /> -4 dice penalty to spot the theft. Flawless Pickpocketing<br /> Technique is also<b> completely immune to magic that detects<br /> Larceny-based actions</b>, <b>unless the user also knows Flawless<br /> Pickpocketing Technique</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like that you mean? A charm that completely invalidates mortals so that they can't beat the Exalt in any way? Is that the kind of supremacy that doesn't exist from 2 charms? Actually, you're right: That's only 1 charm with no pre-reqs. What if we added it's upgrade<b> Stealing from Plain Sight Spirit</b>?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This Charm is similar in all ways to its prerequisite, except that<br /> it allows the Solar to steal an object from plain sight. The<br /> Exalt might swipe a book from a table or take a sword<br /> from a soldier\u2019s scabbard. <b>Such a theft cannot be noticed<br /> for (Solar\u2019s Essence) minutes unless circumstances call<br /> attention to it</b>, such as a soldier attempting to draw his<br /> stolen blade. </div> </div> </div>So you were saying? A 2 charm Larceny exalt can steal the ring off your finger and you literally can't notice for at least one minute. In broad daylight. In front of you. While talking to you.<br /> <br /> Don't even mention <b>Lock Opening Touch</b> and<b> Door-Evading Technique </b>for those unopposed burglaries.<br /> Or <b>Swift Gamblers Eye</b> and <b>Lightning Hand Slight </b>for gamblers.<br /> Or<b> Flawlessly Impenetrable Disguise</b> and <b>Perfect Mirror </b>for disguises<br /> Or S<b>easoned Criminal Method</b> and <b>Spurious Presence </b>for social stealth.<br /> But hey, that's only every 2 charm combo in Larceny that I thought fit the criteria. Do you wanna go to Athletics and Stealth and Ride and Investigate? Do you want to have a 2 charm horse race against an Exalt? A 2 charm contest of strength? a 2 charm climbing challenge? A 2 charm Investigation scene?<br /> <br /> Look I think we've danced this dance enough. Sail is horribly balanced- there are not enough enemies that make it worth heavily investing in. The ST needs to find a way to make it an appropriate challenge, <b>just like every other noncombat skill in the game</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 05-22-2020, 05:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T03:50:42-07:00","id":1390743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390738#post1390738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look I think we've danced this dance enough. Sail is horribly balanced- there are not enough enemies that make it worth heavily investing in. The ST needs to find a way to make it an appropriate challenge, <b>just like every other noncombat skill in the game</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I broadly agree (not about mote regen: you may as well be arguing &quot;Well social influenced used to be called social <i>combat</i> and Gateway is a <i>battle</i> of wits&quot;). Some encounters are meant just as a mote draining speedbump. A heavily invested champion of the gods should beat out Captain Joe Average and his crew of Twenty Normal Dudes.<br /> <br /> But DBs have Charms that explicitly counter Solar perfects (like Trackless Passage Style). A Dog of Unbroken Earth or a Fair Folk Cataphract can contest Flawless Pick Pocketting technique.<br /> <br /> I think Sail is in a worse position than other skills. Same ballpark, different leagues. Foot massage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-22-2020, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T04:01:00-07:00","id":1390745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390743#post1390743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I broadly agree (not about mote regen: you may as well be arguing &amp;quot;Well social influenced used to be called social combat and Gateway is a <i>battle</i> of wits&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Some encounters are meant just as a mote draining speedbump. A heavily invested champion of the gods should beat out Joe Average.<br /> <br /> But DBs have Charms that explicitly counter Solar perfects (like Trackless Passage Style). A Dog of Unbroken Earth or a Fair Folk Cataphract can contest Flawless Pick Pocketting technique.<br /> <br /> I think Sail is in a worse position than other skills. Same ballpark, different leagues. Foot massage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Better change your name to Tony Rocky Horror. <br /> <br /> I'll accept differences on the Sail motes thing, because I consider that to be actual combat. But like I said, I see your reasoning. <br /> <br /> I'm not very familiar with DB and Lunar powersets- but I assume they have Sail charms or something analogous? Armyofwhispers' complaint was that 2 charms in Sail let you effortlessly beat people who <b>don't</b> have sail charms- but as i demonstrated that is not unique to Sail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T06:00:17-07:00","id":1390758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390745#post1390745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not very familiar with DB and Lunar powersets- but I assume they have Sail charms or something analogous?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars have:<br /> <br /> Moon Beckons Tide (adds to the Sail rolls of your allies if they are travelling towards you)<br /> Lodestone Reckoning Manner (adds successes to Sail rolls to navigate a route if you plan the route in advance)<br /> Albatross-and-Hurricane Odyssey (bypasses naval hazards)<br /> Hungry Mouse Mandate (adds a botch to an enemy Sail roll if they are in your territory)<br /> And their Excellency.<br /> <br /> That's it. No double-9s, reroll 6s, plus Essence successes. That's it. Wits+Sail+Specialty+Excellency(+Stunt+Willpower).<br /> <br /> A Dragon-Blooded commander of a trireme tender with five triremes ganging up six-on-one to a Solar can force the Solar to flee (and have no chance of catching them). But they can't do much else. <i>To Solars</i>. Otherwise they have a bunch of cool and interesting powers (starting with +1 success and reroll 6s for 2m and working up from there -- a maxed out Essence 5 DB could throw down a ram with 11+Stunt dice, 4 successes, reroll 6s, double-8s, minus 5 dice on the opponent's roll, plus one Hull damage for 18m 3WP 1a if they win a concealment stratagem first... But they have to win the concealment stratagem first (on 11+Stunt dice with 4 successes, double-9s and reroll 6s for 9m 1WP) and it's once a day).<br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> With 2 dice stunts and +2 ships...<br /> DB Concealment 14 successes<br /> DB Ram 16 success<br /> <br /> Solar Anti-Concealment 22 successes<br /> Solar Anti-Ram 18 successes (or perfectly ignore a Ram for 2m with Superior Positioning Technique)<br /> <br /> Yeah... ok.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-23-2020, 06:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T06:52:56-07:00","id":1390761,"title":"","content":"I think DB captain vs DB captain (if they're built differently, which signature charms are important for), or a DB captain (or several) vs a Lunar Kraken, are probably the most fun naval battles, more than ones with Solars in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T08:21:27-07:00","id":1390775,"title":"","content":"This isn\u2019t necessarily true for all ability trees but the DB sail tree is, in my opinion, less powerful but way cooler than the Solar one. It has really awesome charms that create fog banks or maelstroms out of nowhere, fire a flaming broadside from a ship with no weapons, calling up the wind spirits to fill your sails, stuff like that. <br /> <br /> For any of it to work though, you need to win the naval maneuver roll. Which if you\u2019ve got the right charms gives you disappearing 6s, double 9s, and a dice cap of 6. Compared to a Solars double 9s, disappearing 6s, disappearing 1s, Reflexive reroll all failed dice, +2 non-charm dice for sea devils, +1-3 non charm dice for legendary captain signature, etc. All those really cool powers that the DB has don\u2019t really matter because you can\u2019t ever use them.<br /> <br /> Against a Solar Sail Supernal anyway, they\u2019re awesome against much much less invested Solars or other kinds of creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T20:58:35-07:00","id":1390911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390738#post1390738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's right. Our session this week was online due to Covid, and since we were about to take on the campaign-ending Leviathan (NOT Leviathan from Lunars, whose name is terribly inconvenient), I threw a side story at them. A Fae Noble wants them to fail. This battle was actually designed to be easy to beat- but drain the Eclipse of motes and willpower so he'd be weaker for the &quot;real&quot; challenge.<br /> <br /> That's right. They did not beat the Sail supernal. They didn't stand a chance (go ahead and quote me, forumites), becuase they are not Exalted themselves. They only damaged the ships commanded by the other Solars.<br /> <br /> Yes, which was intentional. The goal for this specific battle- mortals against a Supernal Exalted- was just to drain him of motes and willpower. this was the literal first thing they did in a 5 hour session. After that, the Fae Noble subjected them to individually tailored tests meant to give them Limit and force them to spend Willpower. The design goal of the session was to make them drained, off balance, and tired.<br /> <br /> No, he didnt take any damage. A Supernal going 1 on 2 against talented mortals isn't anything but a speed bump. Mechanics aside, it was really fun though and the player had a great time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool! Glad he had fun!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390738#post1390738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, on one hand I get it. You always want a dynamic system that rewards ingenuity and player agency. OTOH... look man I don't know how many times I can say that's just how Exalted works. if 2 people are gonna keep competing at each other without the system rewarded mechanics of Charms and Excellencies then the one with the bigger dicepool is just going to win. If one side stunts, the other stunts. it's a pure numbers game.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's really... not... though.<br /> <br /> This statement completely ignores the dozens of different ways that a combat character can be built, relying on different strategies, different ways of approaching combat. Solars alone have Evasion focused builds, resistance builds, Melee builds, Archery builds, Survival-pokemon-builds, clinch builds, athletics builds, sorcery builds, and the hundreds of ways you can <i>combine</i> these various things.<br /> <br /> Sail has one: Roll more dice, get more successes.<br /> <br /> In regular combat you can try different strategies to take down an opponent. If he's got high soak, pick off his buddies to gain initiative and then blast him with a decisive. If he's got high parry, hit him with ranged stuff. If he's got high evasion, hit him with area of effect stuff. You can have one guy grapple the target and hold him for a few rounds while your buddies pummel him. You can gang up on one target to pile on the onslaught. Or you can clash him to go toe-to-toe with nothing but the size of your respective dice pools.<br /> <br /> In sail you add more dice and more dice tricks. Your enemies try to gang up on you to reduce your dice pool and generally still get crushed. That combat I simulated up thread? The enemy ships didn't even fire a shot. Not one. They never would have. Sure, a Solar with two melee charms might be able to take on three mortals with comparable dice pools in a fight, but you can be damn sure that the mortals don't die without making a single <i>attack. </i><br /> <br /> I'm not looking for mortals to be the equal of solars, I'm looking for a little bit more than two charm investment to never have to worry about mortals again. I'm looking for a system that supports interesting fights.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390738#post1390738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So first I understand why you and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> argue for 5m/hour, but I feel that the Sailor making opposed sail rolls and maneuvers counts as a turn in combat. At my table that's the ruling.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear, I believe this is a point where the rules are poorly written and I'd also like the system to support 5m/naval combat turn.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390738#post1390738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For your next point- Yes! it would be really easy for a Solar to spend only minimal motes and slowly chip away at his foes. You are right. Which is why, as a Storyteller, I don't let my players have it easy. There's literally hundreds of game design examples on how to challenge players to keep them from being careful and over-cautious. It didn't come up in my battle because my Sail supernal Eclipse goes hard and fast at everything, so he didn't need to be prodded with the stick. But if he sat back and tried to auto-win I would have made the battle harder with weather effects. <i>You might not think that's balanced</i>, and that's fine. STing is an inherently reactive process.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm honestly not sure what you're trying to say here? You seem to be assuming that I believe a ST can't change things in a game once the scene has started. That's kinda silly. and also a strawman argument.<br /> <br /> Of course there are two ways to make a session more interesting when you're in a scene where the PC's are unchallenged: 1. Make things harder by adding complications or 2. Declaring the PCs victorious and moving on to something more interesting.<br /> <br /> My problem is not with how you ST dude. I'm happy to hear your players are having fun. I want a sail system thatis inherently more interesting than more dice = win.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390738#post1390738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I had a Dawn with 15 combat charms, I'd start throwing harder enemies at the party. If I had a Night with Stealth and Larceny charms, they'd eventually run into a DB Sherlock. That doesn't make Sail balanced, I'm not saying it does, but you need to remember that Exalted is not a videogame that can be cheesed by tricking the AI.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, not sure what your point is by saying this.<br /> <br /> My problem with solar sail is not 15 charm investment being the best sailor in the sea. My issue is more:<br /> <br /> a) solar sail ends at Essence 3. To become the best swordsman in the world with all the tricks (if it's <i>not</i> a supernal) you need Essence 5.<br /> <br /> b) A solar with full sail investment will dominate naval combat far more effectively than a Solar with full melee investment can dominate regular combat.<br /> <br /> c) Solar sail charms are cheaper to use than any other combat ability for equivalent effects.<br /> <br /> d) almost <i>no</i> investment makes you exponentially more powerful in sail. Again, <i>this doesn't happen</i> in any other combat ability.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390738#post1390738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By all means, call my Sail Supernal Eclipse player and tell him that playing the invincible sailor and showing off is WrongBadFun. Tell my Twilight that exorcisms below 2nd circle demons are meaningless dice rolls. Not everything has to be a perfectly balanced challenge with meaningful stakes, letting your Exalts roflstomp something with their Supernal can be great fun <i>for the player</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>You keep taking this super personally man. I wish you wouldn't. My issue is not with you. My issue is with the sail system and solar sail. Your player is having fun? Good job! That means you're doing stuff right despite a shitty system.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390738#post1390738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look I think we've danced this dance enough. Sail is horribly balanced- there are not enough enemies that make it worth heavily investing in. The ST needs to find a way to make it an appropriate challenge, <b>just like every other noncombat skill in the game</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I'm actually going to ignore the rest of your post because of the bolded part here. You seem to think that sail is a non-combat skill despite being able to massacre more people per turn than basically any other ability. Ships have crews of dozens or hundreds of people.<br /> <br /> the system is called &quot;Naval Combat&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm not sure why you're trying to pass off sail as a non-combat skill where trivially killing hundreds of people has no more importance than being able to pick someone's pocket without them detecting you (which is no longer automatic if you spend a single mote of excellency, mind, and Flawless Pickpocketing Technique <i>still</i> costs more than most of the dice tricks in sail)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T23:04:15-07:00","id":1390919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390758#post1390758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DB Concealment 14 successes<br /> DB Ram 16 success</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars might not be the only problem if those are the numbers DBs are putting out. They just get to win all the time AND have cool elemental maneuvers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T00:08:53-07:00","id":1390924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390919#post1390919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Solars might not be the only problem if those are the numbers DBs are putting out. They just get to win all the time AND have cool elemental maneuvers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem isn't really the charms its the system which is designed such that anything that doesn't affect maneuver rolls is pretty marginal, any naval-combat charm that didn't include dice-tricks or non-charm dice would be a waste of wordcount. So instead everyone who has naval-combat charms gets to roll as silly number of average successes.<br /> <br /> I also think DB charms were designed with the solar charms in mind, Sea Dragon's Cunning (no prereq.) 3m for double 9s and extra momentum is unusually effective for an E1 DB charm.<br /> <br /> I hope we'll see a lunar sail charm or two in many-faced-strangers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 05-23-2020, 03:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T01:25:49-07:00","id":1390931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390919#post1390919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Solars might not be the only problem if those are the numbers DBs are putting out. They just get to win all the time AND have cool elemental maneuvers.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an Essence 5 DB with maxed stats, the best ship, Stunting, and with literally every published Sail Charm spending 27m 4WP 1a using a 1/scene Charm and a 1/day Charm. I think it's fine.<br /> <br /> (A maxed Lunar (Wits 5d Sail 5d Specialty 1d Excellency 10d Maneuverability 2d Stunt 2d Willpower +1 succcess) is putting out 13 successes (average) for 10m 1WP. (11 successes at 80% confidence.))<br /> <br /> DB 14 successes 9m 1WP<br /> Lunar 13 successes 10m 1WP<br /> Solar 22 successes 6m (if the bonus success from Ocean Conquering Avatar isn't optional, then 21 successes, but 22 successes for 6m 1WP)<br /> <br /> Mortals of Legend (Wits 5 Sail 5 Specialty 1 Trireme 2 Stunt 2 Sail 4 Crew 2 Willpower) 9 successes.<br /> <br /> Armored Kraken (8d+2d Stunt+Willpower) 6 successes (4 successes at 80% confidence). You could comfortably double the Kraken's dice pools -- with 16d the best mortal sailors in the world will <i>probably</i> beat the Kraken if the ST isn't needlessly mean. The Exalted will stomp this great creature of legend but will spend motes to do so (like fighting a Tyrant Lizard on land or some other comparable threat). Whereas the average Realm triarch or Lintha pirate will be consistently dragged to a watery grave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-24-2020, 03:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T10:52:59-07:00","id":1391001,"title":"","content":"The whole thing might work a lot better if instead of having to beat your opponent to generate momentum you could just do it with a naval maneuver roll. That way you don't just get shut down because you keep losing the positioning rolls, and can just try and save up to launch a lucky attack.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doubling the kraken's dicepools sounds like a good start though. Also maybe giving it some ability to start the fight off having already used a concealment action, given the damn thing attacks from directly below the ship.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T12:18:27-07:00","id":1391012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390931#post1390931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Armored Kraken (8d+2d Stunt+Willpower) 6 successes (4 successes at 80% confidence). You could comfortably double the Kraken's dice pools -- with 16d the best mortal sailor in the world (11d) with an outstanding, Argnot level crew (+2d) on a good ship (+2d) spending Willpower (+1 success) will <i>probably</i> beat the Kraken if the ST isn't needlessly mean. The Exalted will stomp this great creature of legend but will spend motes to do so (like fighting a Tyrant Lizard on land or some other comparable threat). Whereas the average Realm triarch or Lintha pirate will be consistently dragged to a watery grave.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes a lot of sense although such a kraken shouldn't be the upper bound for power level of waterborne monsters any more than a tyrant lizard is the top land-based threats (just the top one that a Lunar can transform into). There are all kinds of Wyld behemoths, elemental behemoths, and stranger creatures in Creation's seas that should be potential antagonists for powerful Exalts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391001#post1391001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole thing might work a lot better if instead of having to beat your opponent to generate momentum you could just do it with a naval maneuver roll. That way you don't just get shut down because you keep losing the positioning rolls, and can just try and save up to launch a lucky attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be an improvement although it would make the system less interactive.<br /> <br /> I feel like the system needs to have a little bit more strategic choice to be sufficiently interesting. I have sketched out a system which doesn't go to the full RT / STA complexity, doesn't try to simulate multiple roles on the ship, etc., but is just based around an idea where to block an enemy attack by having more successes you have to be able to predict what attack they're going to make (like you allocate your successes to attacking vs. defending vs. moving and you have to decide what you're defending against). I'm going to try to playtest it at some point and see how it plays.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Doubling the kraken's dicepools sounds like a good start though. Also maybe giving it some ability to start the fight off having already used a concealment action, given the damn thing attacks from directly below the ship. </div> </div> </div>You could give the ship a Perception + Sail roll to notice the signs that a kraken is near in water patterns or something and give the PCs a little bit more time to react.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T12:50:10-07:00","id":1391024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391012#post1391012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This makes a lot of sense although such a kraken shouldn't be the upper bound for power level of waterborne monsters any more than a tyrant lizard is the top land-based threats (just the top one that a Lunar can transform into). There are all kinds of Wyld behemoths, elemental behemoths, and stranger creatures in Creation's seas that should be potential antagonists for powerful Exalts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps HDNP will help with that. Or maybe Exingents.<br /> <br /> I agree in theory. But in practice, I'm not going to homebrew a new kaiju every week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T13:45:21-07:00","id":1391038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391024#post1391024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps HDNP will help with that. Or maybe Exingents.<br /> <br /> I agree in theory. But in practice, I'm not going to homebrew a new kaiju every week.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know this is heresy to some people, but I don't even really agree in theory. Exalted is an epic fantasy game, but sprinting straight up a vertical ship mast, backflipping off the crow's nest, and firing 5 arrows into enemies below before you even hit the ground is epic. That's the kind of things Exalts do just as a matter of course.<br /> <br /> If we're talking about taking one of <a href=\"https://cdna.artstation.com/p/assets/images/images/006/938/130/4k/russell-marks-krakennew.jpg?1502389842\" target=\"_blank\">these</a> and covering it with thick armored plates, fighting that should be at least an eventful afternoon. Not to say that it should be unbeatable by a starting Solar sailor or whatever, it's Exalted. If you want a game system where a Kraken is 100% unbeatable by chargen characters that's DnD's territory. That's a pretty epic actual fight though.<br /> <br /> Then maybe something like <a href=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/lotr/images/f/f4/Dragon_of_the_First_Age_by_rubendevela-0.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20190803194141\" target=\"_blank\">Ancalagon</a> here is the biggest, possibly world ending threat that you face off against maybe once or twice in a campaign, with a lot of campaigns not even getting to that point. If you're facing off against Ancalagon every week, that's a game that I find basically impossible to Storytell for, and also if we're doing that we're not using Exalted, because a lot of systems just do that kind of thing better. Like Godsend from Powered by the Apocalypse, where killing Ancalagon is a diceless action that you can just do at any time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T14:28:17-07:00","id":1391047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391038#post1391038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know this is heresy to some people, but I don't even really agree in theory. Exalted is an epic fantasy game, but sprinting straight up a vertical ship mast, backflipping off the crow's nest, and firing 5 arrows into enemies below before you even hit the ground is epic. That's the kind of things Exalts do just as a matter of course.<br /> <br /> If we're talking about taking one of <a href=\"http://&quot;https://cdna.artstation.com/p/assets/images/images/006/938/130/4k/russell-marks-krakennew.jpg?1502389842&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">these</a> and covering it with thick armored plates, fighting that should be at least an eventful afternoon. Not to say that it should be unbeatable by a starting Solar sailor or whatever, it's Exalted. If you want a game system where a Kraken is 100% unbeatable by chargen characters that's DnD's territory. That's a pretty epic actual fight though.<br /> <br /> Then maybe something like <a href=\"http://&quot;https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/lotr/images/f/f4/Dragon_of_the_First_Age_by_rubendevela-0.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20190803194141&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Ancalagon</a> here is the biggest, possibly world ending threat that you face off against maybe once or twice in a campaign, with a lot of campaigns not even getting to that point. If you're facing off against Ancalagon every week, that's a game that I find basically impossible to Storytell for, and also if we're doing that we're not using Exalted, because a lot of systems just do that kind of thing better. Like Godsend from Powered by the Apocalypse, where killing Ancalagon is a diceless action that you can just do at any time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just as there are big gaps between an Ape and a Blood Ape, then between a Blood Ape and Octavian, then between Octavian and Ligier; I feel like there's room for a kraken as a mundane cryptid, a mystic kraken with overtly magical powers, then the world swallowing Midguard Serpent, then an Elder God from Beyond Reality.<br /> <br /> But Exalted only <i>barely</i> supports &quot;kraken as a cryptid&quot;, and only then if you run them as a pack of three or four kraken.<br /> <br /> Double the kraken's naval pool and you've got a fun encounter. Not an evening, but the highlight of an evening.<br /> <br /> Give it Principle of Motion, The Tower Still Stands and Void Between the Stars, and you've now got a decent mini-boss for your approach to Skullstone. But I'm not going to homebrew that every week.<br /> <br /> But if you want a campaign topper... that just doesn't exist. Maybe you could reskin the volcano monster or something. And if you want an Essence 5 campaign topper, I'm not even sure it's <i>possible</i> to homebrew that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-23-2020, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T15:10:51-07:00","id":1391058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391047#post1391047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Exalted only <i>barely</i> supports &quot;kraken as a cryptid&quot;, and only then if you run them as a pack of three or four kraken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's an issue, I think. I don't want an armored kraken showing up to be the DnD equivalent of encountering a pair of kobold commoners. It's got armor plates that can shrug off a cannonball, and arms large and powerful enough to rip a ship in half.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391047#post1391047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you want a campaign topper... that just doesn't exist. Maybe you could reskin the volcano monster or something. And if you want an Essence 5 campaign topper, I'm not even sure it's <i>possible</i> to homebrew that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I made one once, but it's really, really damn hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T17:47:15-07:00","id":1391081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391047#post1391047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just as there are big gaps between an Ape and a Blood Ape, then between a Blood Ape and Octavian, then between Octavian and Ligier; I feel like there's room for a kraken as a mundane cryptid, a mystic kraken with overtly magical powers, then the world swallowing Midguard Serpent, then an Elder God from Beyond Reality.<br /> <br /> But Exalted only <i>barely</i> supports &quot;kraken as a cryptid&quot;, and only then if you run them as a pack of three or four kraken.<br /> <br /> Double the kraken's naval pool and you've got a fun encounter. Not an evening, but the highlight of an evening.<br /> <br /> Give it Principle of Motion, The Tower Still Stands and Void Between the Stars, and you've now got a decent mini-boss for your approach to Skullstone. But I'm not going to homebrew that every week.<br /> <br /> But if you want a campaign topper... that just doesn't exist. Maybe you could reskin the volcano monster or something. And if you want an Essence 5 campaign topper, I'm not even sure it's <i>possible</i> to homebrew that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I agree that asking the ST to do something like that is not a reasonable expectation. (Thought it might be fun to play a campaign with a lot of encounters where you accept that there will be a lot of half-baked homebrews based on numbers that the ST pulled out of their hat, and have fun figuring out which ones are pushovers, which ones are overpowered and kill you (I guess you would retcon this), which ones never get a chance to use their signature power, etc.) <br /> <br /> I just think it might be cool to have a game with like 1 nontrivial naval encounter per 5 sessions, so 12 total essence 1 to essence 5, of which 4 are exalts, 4 are teams of mortals, and 4 are monsters. I think I as a ST would be down to run that, and prepared to homebrew significantly to make it happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T18:09:31-07:00","id":1391087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391081#post1391081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just think it might be cool to have a game with like 1 nontrivial naval encounter per 5 sessions, so 12 total essence 1 to essence 5, of which 4 are exalts, 4 are teams of mortals, and 4 are monsters. I think I as a ST would be down to run that, and prepared to homebrew significantly to make it happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, what do you mean by non-trivial here? I'm defining trivial as like, no PC ever misses, and the enemy maybe hits like one time in the fight or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T18:31:31-07:00","id":1391090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391087#post1391087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmmm, what do you mean by non-trivial here? I'm defining trivial as like, no PC ever misses, and the enemy maybe hits like one time in the fight or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Wait are we talking about the ordinary combat system now? &quot;Missing&quot; is not really a thing in naval combat.)<br /> <br /> I was thinking &quot;non-trivial&quot; as in from a narrative perspective it seems worth playing out (as opposed to &quot;PCs come upon one ship of mortal pirates, with an interesting person captive onboard&quot; or whatever reason you might have an encounter not worth rolling in your game) and then imagining that the ST would try to make it feel worth playing out from a gameplay perspective as well. <br /> <br /> A basic test for this if the enemy gets to demonstrate what's cool / unique about them. Like if I have an encounter with an enemy dragonblooded captain with a couple cool Charms from the book, or ones I made up myself (let's assume I'm STing), that have awesome elemental manifestations, a key goal for the encounter would be that the DB gets to use at least one but ideally all of their Charms and I get to describe what happens, and the players describe how their PCs deal with it.<br /> <br /> It would be great also if the players get to show off their PC's cool powers, so ideally the enemies are strong enough that it makes those feel worthwhile.<br /> <br /> It would be amazing if the players have to make interesting strategic decisions while all this is going on but this is not a requirement.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T18:40:50-07:00","id":1391092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391090#post1391090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Wait are we talking about the ordinary combat system now? &quot;Missing&quot; is not really a thing in naval combat.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just talking in general, I guess the naval version is just the opponent never getting enough momentum to try anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391090#post1391090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A basic test for this if the enemy gets to demonstrate what's cool / unique about them. Like if I have an encounter with an enemy dragonblooded captain with a couple cool Charms from the book, or ones I made up myself (let's assume I'm STing), that have awesome elemental manifestations, a key goal for the encounter would be that the DB gets to use at least one but ideally all of their Charms and I get to describe what happens, and the players describe how their PCs deal with it..</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the kind of thing I think I'd want to run more than once every month's worth of sessions. If it's a really sail heavy campaign, which most that include Sail at all end up being, I'd like maybe at least once every other session maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T18:57:19-07:00","id":1391094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391092#post1391092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was just talking in general, I guess the naval version is just the opponent never getting enough momentum to try anything.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's the kind of thing I think I'd want to run more than once every month's worth of sessions. If it's a really sail heavy campaign, which most that include Sail at all end up being, I'd like maybe at least once every other session maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was trying to figure out what the minimum for a campaign where the players get to places mainly by sailing there is (the minimum because JohnDoe244 was worried about having to homebrew too much). I would ideally like more, yeah. <br /> <br /> 30 interesting naval encounters in a campaign is probably where it makes sense to go to the full Rogue Trader / Star Trek Adventures style homebrew rather than running every single one as a series of Wits + Maneuverability + Sail rolls.<br /> <br /> (I also think our campaign's sessions may be shorter than other people's, by possibly a factor of 2.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T20:28:10-07:00","id":1391120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390911#post1390911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the system is called &quot;Naval Combat&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have the same problem with the name Social Combat?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My issue is more:a) solar sail ends at Essence 3. To become the best swordsman in the world with all the tricks (if it's <i>not</i> a supernal) you need Essence 5. </div> </div> </div>Melee only has 2 charms over E3: Heaven Sword Flash (E4) and Circle of Bright Reaving (E5). Saying you NEED those charms to be the best swordsman in the world is just false.<br /> <br /> For reference though: Every core book martial art ends at E3 with the exception of Crane, which has one Essence 4 charm. The same is true of War and Stealth and Thrown. Survival only goes into E4 for 2 charms, and they are both in Miracles of the Solar Exalted. Ride ends at 3. Dodge ends at 3. Resistance has a single E4 charm in Miracles, and a single E5 charm. Athletics has 6 charms at E4 and E5. Archery has 4. Thrown has 1. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> b) A solar with full sail investment will dominate naval combat far more effectively than a Solar with full melee investment can dominate regular combat. </div> </div> </div>Agree and Disagree. Look over at the Exalted Arena thread to see how completely one-sided an optimized Solar Melee is. In fact, the Single Point vs Melee boiled down to &quot;if SP doesn't win Join Battle and instantly nova the the Melee to death, they lose&quot;. I do actually agree that the Sail Focused character is more <i>boring</i> though. We'll get back to that line of thought in a second.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> c) Solar sail charms are cheaper to use than any other combat ability for equivalent effects. </div> </div> </div>Yeah probably.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> d) almost <i>no</i> investment makes you exponentially more powerful in sail. Again, <i>this doesn't happen</i> in any other <b>combat </b>ability. </div> </div> </div>It does in War: <b>Immortal Warlord's Tactic</b> has only 1 prereq and it is both a dice trick and an unopposable maneuver.<br /> <br /> I think the problem is that Sail basically exists in a vacuum, wherein the only counter to Sail is Sail, and other posters have pointed out: there really isn't that much to do with Sail. It doesn't cross pollinate the way other combat charms do, and even its closest cousin War already has 1 foot outside the combat skills circle. So I agree with you that Sail isn't great and that Naval Combat isn't great, but I don't agree with you that Sail is somehow unique in this matter, and I don't agree with you that Sail is even a combat ability. Despite seeming on the on the surface like one- people fight and die- it doesn't occupy the same space mechanically as what E3E <i>treats</i> as a combat ability: the incestuous relationship between Melee, Dodge, Brawl, Resistance et al. <br /> <br /> I think unless we resolve this disagreement, &quot;Is Sail actually a combat ability?&quot; we aren't going to really progress much further with our discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T21:33:50-07:00","id":1391128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391120#post1391120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have the same problem with the name Social Combat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really since that's not a thing in 3e<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391120#post1391120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Melee only has 2 charms over E3: Heaven Sword Flash (E4) and Circle of Bright Reaving (E5). Saying you NEED those charms to be the best swordsman in the world is just false.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean three charms in the core. One at essence 4 and two at essence 5. <br /> <br /> And I'd still say that a solar with those charms is a better swordsman than one without.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391120#post1391120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For reference though: Every core book martial art ends at E3 with the exception of Crane, which has one Essence 4 charm. </div> </div> </div> </div>None of which are solar charms so...?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391120#post1391120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">p<br /> The same is true of War and Stealth and Thrown.</div> </div> </div> </div>War ends at essence 3, it's true but thrown has at least one essence 4 charm, and stealth has 3 in the core. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391120#post1391120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Survival only goes into E4 for 2 charms, and they are both in Miracles of the Solar Exalted. Ride ends at 3. Dodge ends at 3. Resistance has a single E4 charm in Miracles, and a single E5 charm. Athletics has 6 charms at E4 and E5. Archery has 4. Thrown has 1. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Considering how far off your counts are in some of these in not gonna go and refute reach one individually.<br /> <br /> I'll say this, there are some abilities that do end at essence 3. They're certainly in the minority though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391120#post1391120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agree and Disagree. Look over at the Exalted Arena thread to see how completely one-sided an optimized Solar Melee is. In fact, the Single Point vs Melee boiled down to &quot;if SP doesn't win Join Battle and instantly nova the the Melee to death, they lose&quot;. I do actually agree that the Sail Focused character is more <i>boring</i> though. We'll get back to that line of thought in a second.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah probably.<br /> <br /> <br /> It does in War: <b>Immortal Warlord's Tactic</b> has only 1 prereq and it is both a dice trick and an unopposable maneuver.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude. Min Essence 2. 4m, 4i, 1wp and can only be used once per battle. This alone would be evidence of how OP solar sail is. <br /> <br /> However you're also either misreading or deliberately misrepresenting this charm. It does NOT provide an unstoppable maneuver. All it does is the dice trick and prevent the opposing player from pulling a specific type of charm out.<br /> <br /> Even if it was a way to win a strategic combat roll unopposed, the next step is to move on to regular combat. You don't just get to kill the opposing army. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391120#post1391120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the problem is that Sail basically exists in a vacuum, wherein the only counter to Sail is Sail, and other posters have pointed out: there really isn't that much to do with Sail. It doesn't cross pollinate the way other combat charms do, and even its closest cousin War already has 1 foot outside the combat skills circle. So I agree with you that Sail isn't great and that Naval Combat isn't great, but I don't agree with you that Sail is somehow unique in this matter, and I don't agree with you that Sail is even a combat ability. Despite seeming on the on the surface like one- people fight and die- it doesn't occupy the same space mechanically as what E3E <i>treats</i> as a combat ability: the incestuous relationship between Melee, Dodge, Brawl, Resistance et al. <br /> <br /> I think unless we resolve this disagreement, &quot;Is Sail actually a combat ability?&quot; we aren't going to really progress much further with our discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's certainly something we can agree on. <br /> <br /> I'm not sure how I could convince you that sail is a combat ability outside of pointing out that:<br /> <br /> A) you can kill more people per turn with sail than any other ability in exalted, without the assistance of magic. <br /> <br /> B) it's the be-all and end-all of a system called naval <b>combat</b><br /> <br /> C) you yourself keep taking about that combat you ran that involved ships where everyone was rolling sail for everything. <br /> <br /> If sail isn't a combat ability, them what combat ability are you using in Naval combat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":8804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","user":"armyofwhispers","date":". 05-24-2020, 12:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T23:38:19-07:00","id":1391136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391058#post1391058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I made one once</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to preface this by saying I love your work, respect you as a person and I think you are the most useful person to me on this forum (excluding the devs but not the writers). But with respect and from a place of love: no you didn't.<br /> <br /> You made a bloated monstrosity of a Primordial, which has yet to be playtested because it's essentially impossible to run.<br /> <br /> Even with a full Circle of players, fighting that thing isn't for a mid-week, after-work gaming sesh. I'd put aside two seven-hour weekend days, with board games on standby... if I wanted to gamble on being the first to run it, which I don't.<br /> <br /> Further, I was talking <i>specifically</i> about a Sail-based boss.<br /> <br /> That said, your Primordial is probably the best end-game Exalted boss ever made -- homebrew or otherwise, across all three editions -- and you should be proud of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-24-2020, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T23:50:22-07:00","id":1391137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391120#post1391120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have the same problem with the name Social Combat?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's specifically called Social Influence now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391120#post1391120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Melee only has 2 charms over E3: Heaven Sword Flash (E4) and Circle of Bright Reaving (E5). Saying you NEED those charms to be the best swordsman in the world is just false.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who's tested a lot of Solar fighters: you really do need those Charms. Especially if fighting Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> Heaven Sword Flash isn't <i>essential</i> in that an Essence 5 Solar with <i>every other</i> Melee Charm can kill Dragon-Blooded three-on-one (six-on-one with Lore and Resistance Charms). But an Essence 1 Starting Solar with Heaven Sword Flash (and Thunderbolt Attack Prana) can kill six DBs <i>in a single blow</i>.<br /> <br /> Circle of Bright Reaving is a bad choice for a Supernal (won't have the motes), but it makes a huge difference for high end combat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391120#post1391120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah probably.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, not &quot;probably&quot;.<br /> <br /> A Lunar spends 10m 1WP for 13 successes.<br /> A Dragon-Blooded spends 27m 4WP 1a for 16 successes.<br /> A Solar spends 6m for 22 successes.<br /> <br /> That's kookoo for coco-puffs crazy better. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It does in War: <b>Immortal Warlord's Tactic</b> has only 1 prereq and it is both a dice trick and an unopposable maneuver.<br /> <br /> I think the problem is that Sail basically exists in a vacuum, wherein the only counter to Sail is Sail </div> </div> </div>If broadside and ram didn't exist, and your options with Sail were &quot;flee or board&quot; then you'd have a fair point here. Then there would be &quot;cross pollination&quot;, and I'd agree with you unreservedly (rather than &quot;broadly&quot;).<br /> <br /> But because Sail exists in a vacuum, Immortal Warlord's Tactic isn't remotely comparable.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Not addressed to anyone specifically, because Exalted 3E is a &quot;natural language&quot; game. But &quot;combat ability&quot; has a specific meaning in Exalted: it's a rules term meaning &quot;Archery, Brawl, Martial Arts, Melee, and Thrown&quot;. Other abilities (Occult, Sail, Athletics, Dodge) can be used to kill people, but they are not &quot;combat abilities&quot; <i>as 3E defines them as a rules term</i>. Likewise some abilities are flagged as being &quot;important in combat&quot; (like Resistance), but they too are not &quot;combat abilities&quot;.<br /> <br /> Neither Sail nor Resistance is a &quot;combat ability&quot;.<br /> <br /> I get why calling Sail a combat ability is useful when discussing Naval Combat *checks title of thread* and we are specifically discussing Naval Combat (and not non-combat uses of Sail). But I'm worried someone new to Exalted is going to get confused if they stumble into us using the wrong terminology.<br /> <br /> Can we all just agree that whilst Sail has non-combat uses, in this thread we are talking specifically about how the Sail ability pertains to the Naval Combat system?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-24-2020, 03:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T06:05:49-07:00","id":1391174,"title":"","content":"So everything else aside, I think we can reach an agreement on the following: Sail is used in Naval Combat to kill other people on boats (among other things). It is both extremely powerful at this, and this power can be attained very cheaply. It is opposed only by other people with Sail. Solars are overwhelmingly better at sail than Non-Solars, in large part because of how powerful and cheap Sail charms are. There are not enough strong naval enemies to make heavy investment in Sail useful.<br /> <br /> So we're all clear on those bits?<br /> <br /> I could go on and on about What Specifically Constitutes a Combat Skill, but that is a subject for its own thread. \u200bI'm sorry I got a little heated. I got wrapped up in the oneupsmanship of forum debates.<br /> <br /> So, Sail is exclusively the skill to use in Naval Combat. There are a couple of ships provided, There's 2 Artifact ships- one Warship and one Flying ship. For Sorceries there's a few to choose from: one makes a small boat from a peach (Floral Ferry), and one lets you sail on the clouds (Keel Cleaves the Clouds). I wouldn't say either are great for combat, Floral Ferry is really fast and has +3 maneuver so its probably best used for boarding actions.<br /> <br /> Sorceries don't really matter in Naval Combat because they are just lumped in to dealing Hull Damage. I had a Twilight Sorcerer use Death of Obsidian Butterflies on an enemy trireme which was cool, but it didn't do any more or less then the artifact harpoon on another ship. Also, considering how... vague a round of positioning is it was really hard to rule on how fast a Sorcerer could summon Sorcerous Motes. Still, 2 damage is better than 1 damage. It requires Resources 3 to obtain first weaponry of similar power, but since you need to own a ship and have crew for any of this to matter, you probably have Resource 3 already, and if you don't that's what piracy is for.<br /> <br /> The artifact warship is called <i>Horizon Endeavor, </i>its in Arms of the Chosen. It costs a whopping <i>10 motes</i> to attune to, but has <b>11 hull points</b>. Eleven! the other ships are 3 or 4. It has a max speed of 14 which is insanely better than the next ship of <i>only 4 </i>(the sorcery <i>Floral Ferry</i> is better at Speed 5 but your call if that's a boat or a spell). It has two special attacks-<u> Red Jade Cannon</u>s deal 1 damage in a broadside attack, but each subsequent turn the opposing ship has to roll to put out the fire or take one hull damage; and <u>Tidecutter Bolts</u> which are basically torpedoes and get bonus damage after a concealment roll.<br /> <br /> The flying ship is the <i>Chariot of Aerial Conquest</i>, which is <u>THE</u> fastest ship in the game at speed 15. It has 6 hull points. It has no special armaments and can hold barely 40 men in tight quarters so it is more like a flying troop transport than an actual ship. It's nigh-invisible in flight (cool), and the soldiers inside have arrow slits to attack from. YMMV on whether this counts as a ship or not, and since it flies and is nearly invisible it probably will never be used in Naval Combat.<br /> <br /> Just as an aside, a ships cruising speed (as in, miles per hour) is its Speed Rating x2, so the super ultra fast <i>Chariot of Aerial</i> <i>Conquest</i> goes along at 30 mph (almost 50 kmph), the <i>Horizon Endeavor</i> is 28 mph (basically the same), both of which roughly tie the spell <i>Cirrus Skiff </i>cast at Essence 5 (30 mph). The sorcery <i>Stormwind Rider</i> is moves one or two people 100 mph, making it the fastest vehicle in the game.<br /> <br /> There's a charm in Sail called <i>Blood and Salt Bondage</i> (Essence 3, 3 prereq charms) which give you and the entire crew a bonus Health Level for every point of Hull that your ship has. Paired with the <i>Horizon Endeavor</i> this will make you <b><i><u>terrifyingly powerful</u></i></b>. This is the equivalent of almost 4 purchases of Ox-Body Technique at Stamina 5. You get the Health Levels of the Ship as your health levels*. The prerequisite charm, <i>Hull-Taming Transformation, </i>lets you take 3 health levels of damage for in lieu of your ship taking 1 hull point of damage. All said and done, you can use your own health to buffer the hull integrity of the <i>Horizon Endeavor</i> from just its own bonus to get 4 free hull points of damage. I'm not kidding when I say <i>nothing in the entire game</i> can rightly challenge your ocean supremacy at this point. Even Fakharu would struggle to harm you, and he can heal himself 3 times in the open ocean.<br /> <br /> The highest level of Sail charms kinda suck by virtue of being sheer overkill and or dicetricks. Death-Daring Maneuver is really cool, but its got the Apocryphal tag because the devs consider it OP. You basically get to invent a natural hazard and then do a straight Wits+Sail roll off to see which of you eats shit. It doesn't specify what exactly it means to &quot;wreck spectacularly&quot;, whether that's instant failure or not, but if you fail you take 2 hull points of damage.<br /> <br /> <i>Ship-Razing Renewal</i> is a full free excellency after wrecking an enemy ship. <i>Rail-Storming Fervor</i> gives you three more Initiative to a JB roll and explicitly can be combo'd with other JB boosters. Interestingly, it doesn't say it <b>has to</b> be used boat-to-boat but I assume that's the intention. The ultimate charm, <i>Black Fathoms Blessed</i> lets you speak Mysterious Ocena Language at other Ocean things and gives you +Maneuverability to Defenses. You also can't drown. eh, kinda weird? It's more for fighting on your ship and dealing with ocean spirits than actually getting into Sail challenges. Special mention to <i>Ship Rolling Juggernaut Method</i> for letting you keep your Momentum after killing an enemy ship, and it gives you a bonus equal to the enemy's Essence. I don't know of any other charms that give you a bonus equal to the enemy's essence, although their probably are many, but that's cool. Its a charm which let's you just steamroll ship after ship, as if you weren't OP enough. This is probably the best charm in all of Sail to just wreck an entire enemy armada. Against an E2 or E3 enemy DB Sail Captain you have basically a free Ram which, at this point, will probably turn out to be an instant death attack. and then you can do it again if you have more momentum. Considering how ludicrous momentum rolls get I wouldn't be surprised if a Sail Master queued up 4 of these in a row: 7-Ess each means you could conceivable hit 4 Wyld Hunt ships one after the other like some kind of ship eating demon. Maybe what they say about anathema is right after all.<br /> <br /> Random thoughts that didn't fit in:<br /> A Lunar with <i>Towering Beast Form</i> as an aquatic animal of Legendary Size doesn't count as a ship, ever, although that would be really goddamn cool. Also there's literally nothing you can do with the Momentum system against submersibles which you think would make an interesting cat-and-mouse game, but then again the Bronze Age isn't really known for anti-submersible battle tactics... but Whaling is a thing and harpoons are a thing so who knows.<br /> <br /> <i>Black Fathoms Blessed</i> requires any ten Sail charms which is the highest number of that thing that I can think of. Integrity one that requires any ten from one ability, not just Integrity, so that qualifies.<br /> <br /> There really ought to be a ship form for Lunars. I mean, Leviathan has been one for like 2 millennia. Has he been paying 5 motes an hour for 2000 years?<br /> <br /> Leviathan's name is really fucking terrible for discussing Giant Sea Monsters without confusion. Seriously, it's just <i>Leviathan</i>. Is there a first age Dawn called <i>Battlegroup</i> we could add to the mix? It should have been something more bronze agey like LVTN (<i>Levantan)</i>. Is there a corresponding <i>Behemoth</i> and <i>Ziz</i>?<br /> <br /> <i>Aerial Chariot</i> has the mechanics of a ship but really isn't one. What use is Maneuver when you can fly and are invisible?<br /> <br /> I misspelled <i>Aerial Chariot</i> as <i>Serial</i> <i>Chariot</i> about 5 times.<br /> <br /> Broadside rules are Resources 3 for regular stuff, and literally no explanation for how to get First Age Anti-ship weaponry or what it is.<br /> <br /> Broadside rules make all catapults, cannons, ballistae, and everything the same flat damage, whether you have two or ten.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Crew&quot; bonus in Sail is +2 if they have an average Sail skill of 4. <i>FOUR</i>. Literally the best sailors alive need to be part of your crew. For reference, that's: <i>The character\u2019s mastery of the Ability sets her above even experts in her field. Seasoned veteran soldiers pale before her prowess; the top physicians of noble families consult her for guidance; clever and wealthy merchants envy her business acumen. </i>And that has to be the <b><i>Average</i></b> skill for them. Are there even 20+ Sail 4 sailors in all of the West?<br /> <br /> Sail does not have a <b><i>This Ability is important in </i></b><i>________, </i>which it shares with Bureaucracy, Investigation, Larceny, Medicine and Survival.<br /> <br /> You'd think there'd be more anti Sea Monster stuff. There's none.<br /> <br /> There's a charm that let's you treat your ship as a familiar for Survival charms.<br /> <br /> There's <i>ONE</i> charm that lets you extend bonuses to your whole fleet.<br /> <br /> Seriously there's like 5 charms about sailing against the wind and one to make a new mast out of anything (despite the lack of sub-system damage), but just one charm to let you have an Armada.<br /> <br /> I probably made at least one person <i>super upset</i> that I interchangably used Boat and Ship a lot in this post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 05-24-2020, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T07:59:07-07:00","id":1391196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391174#post1391174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I probably made at least one person <i>super upset</i> that I interchangably used Boat and Ship a lot in this post.</div> </div> </div> </div>A little. I wouldn't say super.<br /> <br /> I broadly agree.<br /> <br /> You get First Age Weapons by buying/Crafting them as seperate artifacts.<br /> <br /> (And whilst I'm sure The Realm has dozens of Sail 4 characters, they have them as captains of their own ships, not random oarsmen. Likewise I'm are there's at least 20 sailors of legend in the West, but not crammed on the same boat.<br /> <br /> A Lunar could turn into an Armored Kraken. Not a ship, but close enough to interact with the Naval Combat System.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-24-2020, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T14:09:52-07:00","id":1391257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391174#post1391174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So everything else aside, I think we can reach an agreement on the following: Sail is used in Naval Combat to kill other people on boats (among other things). It is both extremely powerful at this, and this power can be attained very cheaply. It is opposed only by other people with Sail. Solars are overwhelmingly better at sail than Non-Solars, in large part because of how powerful and cheap Sail charms are. There are not enough strong naval enemies to make heavy investment in Sail useful.<br /> <br /> So we're all clear on those bits? </div> </div> </div> </div>Sure on all points!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391174#post1391174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could go on and on about What Specifically Constitutes a Combat Skill, but that is a subject for its own thread. \u200bI'm sorry I got a little heated. I got wrapped up in the oneupsmanship of forum debates. </div> </div> </div> </div>It's all good. I get drawn into things the same way. <br /> <br /> As you say, the semantics aside, we all agree that sail is important in Naval Combat. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391174#post1391174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Sail is exclusively the skill to use in Naval Combat. There are a couple of ships provided, There's 2 Artifact ships- one Warship and one Flying ship. For Sorceries there's a few to choose from: one makes a small boat from a peach (Floral Ferry), and one lets you sail on the clouds (Keel Cleaves the Clouds). I wouldn't say either are great for combat, Floral Ferry is really fast and has +3 maneuver so its probably best used for boarding actions.<br /> <br /> Sorceries don't really matter in Naval Combat because they are just lumped in to dealing Hull Damage. I had a Twilight Sorcerer use Death of Obsidian Butterflies on an enemy trireme which was cool, but it didn't do any more or less then the artifact harpoon on another ship. Also, considering how... vague a round of positioning is it was really hard to rule on how fast a Sorcerer could summon Sorcerous Motes. Still, 2 damage is better than 1 damage. It requires Resources 3 to obtain first weaponry of similar power, but since you need to own a ship and have crew for any of this to matter, you probably have Resource 3 already, and if you don't that's what piracy is for. </div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah one of the big issues I have with the sail rules in general is how vaguely they approach things. ALL artillery style, anti ship weaponry being equal unless it's from the first age is pretty weird. Not all artifact weaponry counts as first age tech. Does an artifact weapon do 1 Hull point or 2? (My opinion would be 2 but my point is that it's ambiguous on that point)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391174#post1391174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The artifact warship is called <i>Horizon Endeavor, </i>its in Arms of the Chosen. It costs a whopping <i>10 motes</i> to attune to, but has <b>11 hull points</b>. Eleven! the other ships are 3 or 4. It has a max speed of 14 which is insanely better than the next ship of <i>only 4 </i>(the sorcery <i>Floral Ferry</i> is better at Speed 5 but your call if that's a boat or a spell). It has two special attacks-<u> Red Jade Cannon</u>s deal 1 damage in a broadside attack, but each subsequent turn the opposing ship has to roll to put out the fire or take one hull damage; and <u>Tidecutter Bolts</u> which are basically torpedoes and get bonus damage after a concealment roll. <br /> <br /> The flying ship is the <i>Chariot of Aerial Conquest</i>, which is <u>THE</u> fastest ship in the game at speed 15. It has 6 hull points. It has no special armaments and can hold barely 40 men in tight quarters so it is more like a flying troop transport than an actual ship. It's nigh-invisible in flight (cool), and the soldiers inside have arrow slits to attack from. YMMV on whether this counts as a ship or not, and since it flies and is nearly invisible it probably will never be used in Naval Combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>As you say, the flying chariot is unlikely to be used in direct ship to ship combat, but the naval combat system doesn't really seem to have provided for lots of situations, such as ship to airship or ship to submarine combat. <br /> <br /> And while 15 speed is INSANE compared to any other ship, it doesn't actually do anything once you're in combat. Maneuverability is more important there. Unless you're trying to escape, but I have a hard time believing another ship pursued and caught something with a 15 speed.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391174#post1391174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just as an aside, a ships cruising speed (as in, miles per hour) is its Speed Rating x2, so the super ultra fast <i>Chariot of Aerial</i> <i>Conquest</i> goes along at 30 mph (almost 50 kmph), the <i>Horizon Endeavor</i> is 28 mph (basically the same), both of which roughly tie the spell <i>Cirrus Skiff </i>cast at Essence 5 (30 mph). The sorcery <i>Stormwind Rider</i> is moves one or two people 100 mph, making it the fastest vehicle in the game. <br /> <br /> There's a charm in Sail called <i>Blood and Salt Bondage</i> (Essence 3, 3 prereq charms) which give you and the entire crew a bonus Health Level for every point of Hull that your ship has. Paired with the <i>Horizon Endeavor</i> this will make you <b><i><u>terrifyingly powerful</u></i></b>. This is the equivalent of almost 4 purchases of Ox-Body Technique at Stamina 5-except there's nothing saying what Health Level the charm gives you so I'm inclined to believe they are all -0.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just wanted to address this directly. My read is that you'd gain the exact same health levels as the ship has. So if the so has -0/-1/-4 hl, that's what you'd get. This is purely speculation as the charm itself provides no clarity. They could just as easily have meant for you to get all -4 but they didn't say. I'm not a huge fan of the quality of writing in the solar sail section if that's not clear yet. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391174#post1391174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The prerequisite charm, <i>Hull-Taming Transformation, </i>lets you take 3 health levels of damage for in lieu of your ship taking 1 hull point of damage. All said and done, you can use your own health to buffer the hull integrity of the <i>Horizon Endeavor</i> from just its own bonus to get 4 free hull points of damage. I'm not kidding when I say <i>nothing in the entire game</i> can rightly challenge your ocean supremacy at this point. Even Fakharu would struggle to harm you, and he can heal himself 3 times in the open ocean. </div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely agree with you that this combo would make you damn near untouchable. It's really unfortunate that they've set the bar this high for artifact vs mundane ships as well. Artifact weapons and armor don't get this big of a boost vs the mundane equivalent but there's the issue of scale here as well. <br /> <br /> To me this is closer to the jump from mundane armor to a warstrider. I'm not even sure if that's inappropriate, I'm just pointing it out.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391174#post1391174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The highest level of Sail charms kinda suck by virtue of being sheer overkill and or dicetricks. Death-Daring Maneuver is really cool, but its got the Apocryphal tag because the devs consider it OP. You basically get to invent a natural hazard and then do a straight Wits+Sail roll off to see which of you eats shit. It doesn't specify what exactly it means to &amp;quot;wreck spectacularly&amp;quot;, whether that's instant failure or not, but if you fail you take 2 hull points of damage. </div> </div> </div> </div>I would love for solar sail to include more shit like this. Not the creating a hazard part, but the causing damage to your enemies by sailing through the deadly hazard type stuff. <br /> <br /> I want to be able to fly the millennium falcon through an asteroid field to shake off pursuers, that type of high stakes dramatic stuff. What we've got doesn't even let two ships trade broadsides while they sail past one another.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391174#post1391174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Ship-Razing Renewal</i> is a full free excellency after wrecking an enemy ship. <i>Rail-Storming Fervor</i> gives you three more Initiative to a JB roll and explicitly can be combo'd with other JB boosters. Interestingly, it doesn't say it <b>has to</b> be used boat-to-boat but I assume that's the intention. The ultimate charm, <i>Black Fathoms Blessed</i> lets you speak Mysterious Ocena Language at other Ocean things and gives you +Maneuverability to Defenses. You also can't drown. eh, kinda weird? It's more for fighting on your ship and dealing with ocean spirits than actually getting into Sail challenges. Special mention to <i>Ship Rolling Juggernaut Method</i> for letting you keep your Momentum after killing an enemy ship, and it gives you a bonus equal to the enemy's Essence. I don't know of any other charms that give you a bonus equal to the enemy's essence, although their probably are many, but that's cool. Its a charm which let's you just steamroll ship after ship, as if you weren't OP enough. This is probably the best charm in all of Sail to just wreck an entire enemy armada. Against an E2 or E3 enemy DB Sail Captain you have basically a free Ram which, at this point, will probably turn out to be an instant death attack. and then you can do it again if you have more momentum. Considering how ludicrous momentum rolls get I wouldn't be surprised if a Sail Master queued up 4 of these in a row: 7-Ess each means you could conceivable hit 4 Wyld Hunt ships one after the other like some kind of ship eating demon. Maybe what they say about anathema is right after all. </div> </div> </div> </div>Front have much to add here. This sums up a lot of issues with high end sail. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391174#post1391174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random thoughts that didn't fit in: <br /> A Lunar with <i>Towering Beast Form</i> as an aquatic animal of Legendary Size doesn't count as a ship, ever, although that would be really goddamn cool. Also there's literally nothing you can do with the Momentum system against submersibles which you think would make an interesting cat-and-mouse game, but then again the Bronze Age isn't really known for anti-submersible battle tactics... but Whaling is a thing and harpoons are a thing so who knows. </div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah the fact that aquatic animals of legendary size don't normally interact with the naval system at all is a definite gap imo. I think I'd give most of them some kind of naval maneuvering stuff similar to armored kraken. <br /> <br /> I'd love to see lunar charms that key off of these systems. Maybe if we ever get an in depth write-up for Leviathan, himself? <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391174#post1391174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Black Fathoms Blessed</i> requires any ten Sail charms which is the highest number of that thing that I can think of. Integrity one that requires any ten from one ability, not just Integrity, so that qualifies. <br /> <br /> There really ought to be a ship form for Lunars. I mean, Leviathan has been one for like 2 millennia. Has he been paying 5 motes an hour for 2000 years?<br /> <br /> Leviathan's name is really fucking terrible for discussing Giant Sea Monsters without confusion. Seriously, it's just <i>Leviathan</i>. Is there a first age Dawn called <i>Battlegroup</i> we could add to the mix? It should have been something more bronze agey like LVTN (<i>Levantan)</i>. Is there a corresponding <i>Behemoth</i> and <i>Ziz</i>? </div> </div> </div> </div>Yup... Sigh<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391174#post1391174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Aerial Chariot</i> has the mechanics of a ship but really isn't one. What use is Maneuver when you can fly and are invisible?<br /> <br /> I misspelled <i>Aerial Chariot</i> as <i>Serial</i> <i>Chariot</i> about 5 times. <br /> <br /> Broadside rules are Resources 3 for regular stuff, and literally no explanation for how to get First Age Anti-ship weaponry or what it is. <br /> <br /> Broadside rules make all catapults, cannons, ballistae, and everything the same flat damage, whether you have two or ten. <br /> <br /> The &amp;quot;Crew&amp;quot; bonus in Sail is +2 if they have an average Sail skill of 4. <i>FOUR</i>. Literally the best sailors alive need to be part of your crew. For reference, that's: <i>The character\u2019s mastery of the Ability sets her above even experts in her field. Seasoned veteran soldiers pale before her prowess; the top physicians of noble families consult her for guidance; clever and wealthy merchants envy her business acumen. </i>And that has to be the <b><i>Average</i></b> skill for them. Are there even 20+ Sail 4 sailors in all of the West? </div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah the requirements for the crew bonus are pretty ridiculous. Also an issue to my mind is that even if you have a crew composed entirely of water elementals or water aspect Dragon bloods, they're no better to you than mortals with high training. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391174#post1391174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sail does not have a <b><i>This Ability is important in </i></b><i>________, </i>which it shares with Bureaucracy, Investigation, Larceny, Medicine and Survival. </div> </div> </div> </div>It's true, though I will point out that the sail subsystem interacts with no other ability, and no other ability is important to the sail subsystem (at least not outside of stuff like perception + awareness rolls to spot another ship or something like that). Navigation? Sail. Combat? Sail. Maneuvering? Sail. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391174#post1391174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd think there'd be more anti Sea Monster stuff. There's none. <br /> <br /> There's a charm that let's you treat your ship as a familiar for Survival charms. </div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, there is? Which one? <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391174#post1391174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's <i>ONE</i> charm that lets you extend bonuses to your whole fleet. <br /> <br /> Seriously there's like 5 charms about sailing against the wind and one to make a new mast out of anything (despite the lack of sub-system damage), but just one charm to let you have an Armada. </div> </div> </div> </div>And sailing against the wind is PURE st fiat. There are no mechanics to figure out what speed bonus to apply in combat I'd you're trying an escape maneuver. All positioning or direction stuff is abstracted out<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391174#post1391174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I probably made at least one person <i>super upset</i> that I interchangably used Boat and Ship a lot in this post.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T12:30:28-07:00","id":1391527,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I made (with help) a first draft of an alternative naval system.<br /> <br /> Design goals:</span></span></span><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The system should a little more complicated than the existing system, but not a huge amount more.</li> <li>In a fight between opponents that are evenly matched, or close to it, there should be some nonobvious strategic decisions.</li> <li>A fight between evenly matched opponents should not last forever.</li> <li>In a fight against a weaker opponent, it should not be trivial to shut down their attacks and emerge unscathed. Doing this requires some combination of luck, good strategy, and a substantially larger dice pool.</li> </ol><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Not design goals:</span></span></span><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>I didn\u2019t try to make the system compatible with existing Charms or naval enemies - largely because most of the existing content (the Solar charmset and the Armored Kraken) do not seem very well balanced.</li> <li>I didn\u2019t try to simulate the complexity of running a ship, including the reliance on mortal crew, or ensure every player has something to do. This is not designed for campaigns with huge amounts of naval combat.</li> <li>I didn't try to make rules for all the cool stuff that could go in the basic combat system (like concealment or staying upwind), although I did try to build a framework that this could be added to in a reasonable way.</li> </ol><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><br /> I playtested it once, between Exalts with Solar-like Excellencies but no Charms, in a total white room with no narrative enhancements, and had fun. That's not much data but <br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>The system:</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Naval combat proceeds in rounds. At the beginning of each round, each ship\u2019s captain declares an enemy ship to target, and then makes a Naval Maneuver roll (Wits + Sail + Maneuverability). They declare Charms associated to this roll publicly, before rolling, but keep the successes secret. They take the obtained successes and then divide them up between Attack, Defense, Strategy, and Positioning pools. All captains simultaneously reveal their allocations, and the round plays out.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Naval combat uses a resource, Momentum, as well as a range band system - ship can be at a close range, normal range, or long range from each other. Combat usually starts at normal range.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">To put any points in their attack pool, a captain must have at least 1 Momentum. They also must declare what weapon they are attacking with. See below for typical ship weapons.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">A naval combat round proceeds to Attack, Positioning, and Strategy steps.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Attack step: </b>Every ship that has more points in their Attack pool than their target has in their Defense pool makes a successful attack. They add their Momentum to their weapon bonus, divide by four, and round down. The defending ship takes that many levels of hull damage. Their Momentum is then reset to zero. Every ship that has no more successes in their Attack pool than the target has in their Defense pool misses, and loses half their Momentum, rounding down.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Weapon types:</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Catapaults and ballistae may be used at close range or normal range. Their weapon bonus is 0 for average quality, +1 for high quality, and -1 for low quality. They also get +1 for a great number of weapons, 0 for a usual number, or -1 for a small number. Artifact weapons can have a higher weapon bonus.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ramming prows may be used only at close range. Their power comes from speed, and their weapon bonus is the number of extra successes in the attack poll beyond the target\u2019s defense pool (thus, it is always at least one). A ship without a ramming prow may ram, using the body of the ship as a weapon, but it is a desperation move - their ship takes equal damage.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">A sorcerer with appropriate training is a weapon in themselves - their weapon bonus is their Occult rating.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Boarding is also treated as a type of attack, which can be taken from close range. It requires 10 Momentum, minus the target\u2019s current damage penalty.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Positioning step: </b>In a duel between ships, whoever got a higher Positioning pool, if any, chooses how to position their two ships. They may move their ship one range band closer or further. They may instead take advantage of a terrain feature, such as concealing their ship in a fog bank, which has its own special rules.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">For two or more steps, whoever has the highest Positioning pool chooses a direction first, and then the next, going through everyone who had a success in their positioning pool, with the restriction that later choices must be consistent with earlier ones. For instance, if the captain with the highest Position roll chose to move closer to an enemy ship, that enemy ship could not choose to move further away, or maintain their distance, but they could go into a fog bank, and the captain of another enemy ship would be unaffected.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ties are broken by the average Wits + Sail of the ship\u2019s crew, and then randomly.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">A ship at long range from all enemy ships that chooses to move further escapes the combat. However, they must have 8 Momentum to do this. If they are pursued, they roll opposed Wits + Sail + Speed with their pursuer, and if they roll lower, must begin naval combat again. This resets Momentum, and combat begins again at normal range.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Strategy step:</b> Each ship\u2019s Strategy pool is added to their Momentum. Unlike in normal combat, motes are not recovered in naval combat.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><br /> <b>Notes on ships:</b><br /> <br /> All numerics very subject to change but a standard combat ship has the same health levels as a normal human and maneuverability +0. Lighting ballistae have a +4 weapon bonus and implosion bows have +5.</span></span></span><br /> </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T13:24:10-07:00","id":1391536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391174#post1391174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There really ought to be a ship form for Lunars. I mean, Leviathan has been one for like 2 millennia. Has he been paying 5 motes an hour for 2000 years?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I totally agree with pretty much everything you state here, but I would like to point out that at E4 Lunars can get a charm to waive the recurring Legendary Size costs.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to point out that even though an Armored Kraken has a Naval Maneuver pool, it doesn't say anywhere what (Attribute + Ability) roll that is. I guess it's probably (Wits + Sail), but it's weird to me that a sea monster would need to know how to sail in order to break a ship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24587-yamajin","name":"Yamajin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24587_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T14:09:14-07:00","id":1391547,"title":"","content":"QCs don't breakdown what the source of their dice-pool ratings are. They're just assigned whatever ratings feel appropriate to allow them to function in their designed space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T14:44:29-07:00","id":1391556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391547#post1391547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">QCs don't breakdown what the source of their dice-pool ratings are. They're just assigned whatever ratings feel appropriate to allow them to function in their designed space.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is a hassle for Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T15:10:52-07:00","id":1391560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yamajin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391536#post1391536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, I totally agree with pretty much everything you state here, but I would like to point out that at E4 Lunars can get a charm to waive the recurring Legendary Size costs.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to point out that even though an Armored Kraken has a Naval Maneuver pool, it doesn't say anywhere what (Attribute + Ability) roll that is. I guess it's probably (Wits + Sail), but it's weird to me that a sea monster would need to know how to sail in order to break a ship.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It feels reasonable to me that a Lunar transformed into an Armored Kraken would roll Wits + Sail, which is the most relevant question. There seems to substantial overlap in the knowledge - like, catching up with a ship it would help to know how ships move, and stuff about wind and ocean currents. It also feels thematic.<br /> <br /> What would be the other most reasonable choice? Wits + Athletics?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T16:30:28-07:00","id":1391566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391560#post1391560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It feels reasonable to me that a Lunar transformed into an Armored Kraken would roll Wits + Sail, which is the most relevant question. There seems to substantial overlap in the knowledge - like, catching up with a ship it would help to know how ships move, and stuff about wind and ocean currents. It also feels thematic.<br /> <br /> What would be the other most reasonable choice? Wits + Athletics?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Much like how Ride replaces Athletics when you're mounted, I'd say that Athletics should replace sail when you're transformed into an aquatic monstrosity. <br /> <br /> Swimming through the water is normally Dex + Athletics (depending on what you're trying to do) but you've still got to out wit the naval opponent somewhat. So wits + Athletics would be my call","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T01:36:26-07:00","id":1391649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1391090#post1391090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Wait are we talking about the ordinary combat system now? &quot;Missing&quot; is not really a thing in naval combat.)<br /> <br /> I was thinking &quot;non-trivial&quot; as in from a narrative perspective it seems worth playing out (as opposed to &quot;PCs come upon one ship of mortal pirates, with an interesting person captive onboard&quot; or whatever reason you might have an encounter not worth rolling in your game) and then imagining that the ST would try to make it feel worth playing out from a gameplay perspective as well.<br /> <br /> A basic test for this if the enemy gets to demonstrate what's cool / unique about them. Like if I have an encounter with an enemy dragonblooded captain with a couple cool Charms from the book, or ones I made up myself (let's assume I'm STing), that have awesome elemental manifestations, a key goal for the encounter would be that the DB gets to use at least one but ideally all of their Charms and I get to describe what happens, and the players describe how their PCs deal with it.<br /> <br /> It would be great also if the players get to show off their PC's cool powers, so ideally the enemies are strong enough that it makes those feel worthwhile.<br /> <br /> It would be amazing if the players have to make interesting strategic decisions while all this is going on but this is not a requirement.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure I've said this thing a thousand times. But this should be the baseline for Exalted, the fact that it was not included and thought directly in the the Exalted 3e Core Book was a terrible mistake, and I really really hope Crucible of Legends will fix this to some extend (or Exalted Essence, at least).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}